0000                             ; =============================================================================
0000                             ;  B8Script interpreter for the Z80
0000                             ;  Spec: docs/b8script.md (2026-11-23).
0000                             ; 
0000                             ;  Four switches, set in the EQU lines below:
0000                             ;    CPM      0 = generic ROM build (KEY/CONOUT at fixed addresses)
0000                             ;             1 = CP/M 2.2 .COM file: loads the file named on the command line
0000                             ;    EDITOR   1 = with the line editor built in (see the end of this file):
0000                             ;                 the spec's suggested standard. It goes with either setting
0000                             ;                 of the other two.
0000                             ;    CHECKED  0 = no checks (spec: the programmer is responsible)
0000                             ;             1 = starts with every variable at 0 and every word undefined,
0000                             ;                 and stops on every error in the spec's table (and Ctrl-C)
0000                             ;                 with a three-line report: the letter and the place as
0000                             ;                 line and column, and both stacks. See `error`.
0000                             ;    ANSI     1 = the four console codes (`@ `^ `_ `?) send ANSI escape
0000                             ;                 sequences through CONOUT
0000                             ;             0 = they call four routines of the machine's own instead:
0000                             ;                 CONAT, CONCLS, CONEOL and CONCUR (see the equates)
0000                             ; 
0000                             ;  In every build Ctrl-C stops a running program (an unchecked build stops
0000                             ;  without a word): see the console layer for the rules, the held key and
0000                             ;  the break-off cell.
0000                             ; 
0000                             ;  Assembler: asm80 (https://maly.github.io/asm80-node/), Z80 mode.
0000                             ; =============================================================================
0000                CPM:      EQU   1   ; 1 = CP/M .COM build
0000                CHECKED:   EQU   0   ; 1 = checked build
0000                EDITOR:   EQU   0   ; 1 = with the line editor
0000                ANSI:     EQU   1   ; 1 = the console codes send ANSI sequences
0000                EDGEN:    EQU   EDITOR*(1-CPM)   ; (the generic build with the editor)
0000                             ; (IF takes any value but 0 as true, so
0000                             ;  IF CHECKED+EDITOR means "either")
0000                TABP0:    EQU   EDGEN*(1-CHECKED)   ; (the build with its table in page zero)
0000                             ; -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
0000                             ;  Register use, everywhere in the interpreter
0000                             ; 
0000                             ;    BC   IP: the address of the next program character to read
0000                             ;    HL   TOS: the top data-stack cell is kept here, not in memory
0000                             ;    SP   the data stack: (SP) is NOS, the cell under TOS. The data stack is
0000                             ;         the Z80"s own stack, which is what the spec"s machine-code contract
0000                             ;         needs ("the data cells above the return address").
0000                             ;    HL'  return-stack pointer (the alternate HL). Entries are 2 bytes; the
0000                             ;         stack grows down. Only rpop and rpushn (and the checks) touch it.
0000                             ;    A DE scratch. Every handler is entered with HL = TOS and may use A, DE.
0000                             ; 
0000                             ;  One-byte calls. The routines used most are reached with RST, one byte
0000                             ;  instead of three:
0000                             ; 
0000                             ;    RST 08h  rpop    pop the return stack into DE
0000                             ;    RST 18h  drop    drop TOS, then next character     (ends a handler)
0000                             ;    RST 20h  neg16   HL = -HL
0000                             ;    RST 28h  putc    print A
0000                             ;    RST 30h  next    next character                    (ends a handler)
0000                             ; 
0000                             ;  RST 18h and RST 30h never return: an RST is a CALL, so the first thing
0000                             ;  each of them does is POP DE to throw the return address away.
0000                             ; 
0000                             ;  The CP/M build can't own page zero, so the block from `vecs` to `vecend`
0000                             ;  (image addresses 0108h-0133h) is copied to 0008h-0033h when it starts. The
0000                             ;  code in that block is written to work at either place.
0000                             ; 
0000                             ;  Dispatch. PTAB holds one byte per punctuation character: the low byte of
0000                             ;  its handler's address. The high byte is worked out from the character:
0000                             ;  the handlers of the first NPG1 characters (in code order) start in the
0000                             ;  image's second page, the rest in its first. The layout below keeps to
0000                             ;  that, and testing/chktab.py checks it in every build.
0000                             ; -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
0000                             ;  Memory map. Everything the interpreter writes is in four RAM pages:
0000                             ; 
0000                             ;    RSPAGE   return stack, 112 entries (the pointer stays inside this page)
0000                             ;    DSPAGE   data stack, 127 cells (the top four bytes of the page are spare,
0000                             ;             so a full stack runs two bytes into the page below)
0000                             ;    LETPAGE  letter cells: A..Z at +00h..+33h, a..z at +40h..+73h (so a word
0000                             ;             cell is always 64 bytes below its variable), the heap pointer at
0000                             ;             +7Ch, interpreter variables in the gaps, and the -n? line buffer
0000                             ;             at +80h..+FFh
0000                             ;    PROG     the program text, NUL-terminated; the heap starts after the NUL
0000                             ; 
0000                             ;  The stacks sit below the letter page, so "the program's own space" (what
0000                             ;  the checked build lets ! and . write) is the single range from the letter
0000                             ;  page up to the heap limit. Each stack has a guard band: the data stack can
0000                             ;  overrun by a cell or two (and the calls made while it is full, the error
0000                             ;  report's included) into the top 32 bytes of the return-stack page, which
0000                             ;  are never used, and the return stack by one entry into the page below it.
0000                             ; -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
0000                          IF   CPM   
0000                BDOS:     EQU   0005h   
0000                BASE:     EQU   0100h   ; where the image starts
0000                          ENDIF      
0000                          IF   CPM*(1-EDITOR)   
0000                EXIT:     EQU   0000h   ; warm boot
0000                          ENDIF      
0000                          IFN   CPM   
                                 ; ---- generic machine: edit these to suit -----------------------------------
                    KEY:      EQU   0FF06h   ; a waiting key in A, or A = 0 if none is
                                 ;   waiting. The zero flag must match A
                                 ;   (end the routine with OR A / RET).
                    CONOUT:   EQU   0FF03h   ; print the character in A
                                 ;   KEY and CONOUT must preserve BC, DE, HL and HL'.
                    RSPAGE:   EQU   80h   ; 8000h return stack
                    DSPAGE:   EQU   81h   ; 8100h data stack
                    LETPAGE:   EQU   82h   ; 8200h letter cells and line buffer
                    PROG:     EQU   8300h   ; where the loader puts the program text
                    HEAPLIM:   EQU   0F0h   ; the heap must stay below F000h (a page)
                    BASE:     EQU   0000h   ; where the image starts
0000                          ENDIF      
0000                          IF   (1-CPM)*(1-ANSI)   
                                 ; ---- generic machine with ANSI = 0: the console codes call these ------------
                    CONAT:    EQU   0FF0Ch   ; `@  cursor to row E, column L, both from 0
                                 ;     (DE and HL hold the whole cells). May
                                 ;     change A, DE and HL
                    CONCLS:   EQU   0FF0Fh   ; `^  clear the screen and home the cursor
                    CONEOL:   EQU   0FF12h   ; `_  clear from the cursor to the end of the line
                    CONCUR:   EQU   0FF15h   ; `?  cursor off if A = 0 (the zero flag is set
                                 ;     to match), on if not. May change A, DE, HL
                                 ;   All four must preserve BC and HL'; CONCLS and CONEOL also DE and HL.
0000                          ENDIF      
0000                          IF   (1-CPM)*(1-EDITOR)   
                    EXIT:     EQU   0FF09h   ; where to go when the program ends
0000                          ENDIF      
0000                          IF   EDGEN   
                    LEAVE:    EQU   0FF09h   ; where the editor's ^X goes
0000                          ENDIF      
0000                          IF   EDITOR*CPM   
                    LEAVE:    EQU   0000h   ; the editor's ^X: warm boot
0000                          ENDIF      
0000                          IF   EDITOR   
                    EXIT:     EQU   edend   ; a program that ends goes back to the editor,
                    SKEND:    EQU   skend   ;   also when it ends inside skip
0000                          ENDIF      
0000                          IF   1-EDITOR   
0000                SKEND:    EQU   EXIT   
0000                          ENDIF      
0000                MSLOOP:   EQU   40   ; n? inner loop count for about 1 ms (1-255):
0000                             ; each pass calls getk once, so tune it for
0000                             ; your clock and your KEY routine. (The wait
0000                             ; for a second Ctrl-C uses it too: 250 ms.)
0000                             ; letter-page layout (offsets inside LETPAGE)
0000                LET:      EQU   LETPAGE*256   
0000                HEAP:     EQU   LET+7Ch   ; the heap pointer
0000                RSAVE:    EQU   LET+34h   ; gap after Z: return stack pointer, saved
0000                             ;   around machine code;
0000                NPEND:    EQU   LET+38h   ;   minus the address of the program's end
0000                             ;   (the heap"s first byte), for the checked "_';
0000                EDLN:     EQU   LET+3Ah   ;   the editor: the number of the line that ^E
0000                             ;   put in the input line (0: none)
0000                SEED:     EQU   LET+76h   ; gap after z: the random seed, the cell whose
0000                             ;   address `. gives. Nothing sets it at the
0000                             ;   start but the checked build's clearing;
0000                KEYBUF:   EQU   LET+7Ah   ;   a key read by the break check and
0000                             ;   held for the next "?" (0: none);
0000                BRKOFF:   EQU   LET+7Bh   ;   the break-off cell: a program that stores a
0000                             ;   non-zero byte here gets Ctrl-C as a key
0000                LBHDR:    EQU   LET+7Eh   ; CP/M BDOS 10 header: max, count
0000                LINEBUF:   EQU   LET+80h   ; -n? text, ending in CR
0000                RSTOP:    EQU   RSPAGE*256+0E0h   ; empty return stack: the 32 bytes above it
0000                             ; take calls made while the data stack is full
0000                DSTOP:    EQU   DSPAGE*256+0FCh   ; empty data stack. The four bytes above it
0000                             ; are spare: a character can pop two cells
0000                             ; too many before the checked build sees it,
0000                             ; and the next call must not land on the
0000                             ; letter cells.
0000                             ; =============================================================================
0000                             ;  The first 49 bytes: the entry, then the RST routines, with small handlers
0000                             ;  and routines filling the gaps between them. Generic: this IS page zero.
0000                             ;  CP/M: it is the start of the .COM file, and 0108h-0133h is also copied to
0000                             ;  page zero (see the header).
0000                             ; =============================================================================
0100                          .ORG   BASE   
0100                          IF   (1-CPM)*(1-EDITOR)*CHECKED   
                              XOR   A   ; 00  reset. (This byte, AFh, is also what an
0100                          ENDIF      ;     undefined word runs into: see e_hi.)
0100                          IF   1-EDGEN   
0100   31 FC 06               LD   SP,DSTOP   ; 00  reset, or the start of the .COM file
0103                          ENDIF      
0103                          IF   (1-CPM)*(1-EDITOR)*(1-CHECKED)   
                              LD   BC,PROG   ; 03  the IP
                              JR   st0   ; 06  (the rest of the startup is close by)
0103                          ENDIF      
0103                          IF   (1-CPM)*(1-EDITOR)*CHECKED   
                              JR   init   ; 04  (the rest of the startup is close by)
                              DW   0   ; 06  spare
0103                          ENDIF      
0103                          IF   EDGEN   
                              XOR   A   ; 00  reset: no program yet. (This byte, AFh,
                              LD   (PROG),A   ;     is also what an undefined word runs
                              JP   init   ; 04  into in the checked build: see e_hi.)
                              NOP      ; 07  spare
0103                          ENDIF      
0103                          IF   CPM   
0103   C3 C5 04               JP   start   ; 03
0106   00 00                  DW   0   ; 06  spare
0108                          ENDIF      
0108                VECS:        
0108                             ; ---- RST 08h: rpop: pop the return stack into DE ---------------------------
0108   D9           RPOP:     EXX      ; 08
0109   5E                     LD   E,(HL)   
010A   23                     INC   HL   
010B   56                     LD   D,(HL)   
010C   23                     INC   HL   
010D   D5                     PUSH   DE   ; across to the main registers
010E   D9                     EXX      
010F   D1                     POP   DE   
0110   C9                     RET      ; 10  (so RST 10h is not used)
0111                             ; ctl: the inner loop comes here for characters below 21h. A = c - 21h.
0111   C6 21        CTL:      ADD   A,21h   ; 11  back to c; zero only for NUL
0113   20 1F                  JR   NZ,next0   ;     the rest are ignored
0115   C3 00 00     ENDPROG:   JP   EXIT   ;     the program has ended
0118                             ; ---- RST 18h: drop TOS, then next ------------------------------------------
0118   D1           RST18:    POP   DE   ; 18  discard the RST's return address
0119   E1                     POP   HL   ;     new TOS = NOS
011A   18 15                  JR   nx   
011C   E5           H_FROMR:   PUSH   HL   ; 1C  "}" return stack to TOS
011D   CF                     RST   08h   
011E   EB                     EX   DE,HL   
011F   F7                     RST   30h   
0120                             ; ---- RST 20h: neg16: HL = -HL (keeps BC, DE) -------------------------------
0120   AF           NEG16:    XOR   A   ; 20
0121   95                     SUB   L   
0122   6F                     LD   L,A   
0123   9F                     SBC   A,A   
0124   94                     SUB   H   
0125   67                     LD   H,A   
0126   C9                     RET      
0127   00                     NOP      ; 27  spare
0128                             ; ---- RST 28h: putc: print A (keeps BC, DE, HL, HL') ------------------------
0128                RST28:       
0128                          IFN   CPM   
                    PUTC:     JP   CONOUT   ; 28
0128                          ENDIF      
0128                          IF   CPM   
0128   C3 AC 04               JP   putc   ; 28
012B                          ENDIF      
012B   E9           JPHL:     JP   (HL)   ; 2B  (for the machine-code call)
012C   E3           H_TOR:    EX   (SP),HL   ; 2C  "{" TOS to the return stack: the new TOS
012D   C3 C1 01               JP   rpushn   ;     comes up, the old one goes across
0130                             ; ---- RST 30h: next character -----------------------------------------------
0130   D1           RST30:    POP   DE   ; 30  discard the RST's return address
0131                NX:          
0131                          IF   CPM   
0131   C3 34 01               JP   next0   ; (this copy runs in page zero)
0134                          ENDIF      
0134                VECEND:      
0134                             ; =============================================================================
0134                             ;  The inner loop: read one character and sort it by range.
0134                             ; 
0134                             ;    00h          end of program
0134                             ;    01h-20h, 7Fh-FFh   ignored (control, space, DEL, high bytes)
0134                             ;    30h-39h      digit: read a whole number
0134                             ;    41h-5Ah      A-Z: call the word in that letter's cell
0134                             ;    61h-7Ah      a-z: push the address of that letter's cell
0134                             ;    the rest     punctuation: jump through PTAB, 32 entries, in code order
0134                             ; =============================================================================
0134                NEXT0:       
0134                          IF   CHECKED   
                              CALL   chkstk   ; both stacks are checked once per character
0134                          ENDIF      
0134   0A                     LD   A,(BC)   
0135   03                     INC   BC   
0136   D6 21                  SUB   21h   ; A = c - 21h
0138   38 D7                  JR   C,ctl   ; c < 21h: NUL ends, the rest are ignored
013A   FE 0F                  CP   0Fh   
013C   38 22                  JR   C,punct   ; 21h-2Fh: PTAB index 0-14
013E   D6 0F                  SUB   0Fh   ; A = c - 30h
0140   FE 0A                  CP   0Ah   
0142   38 67                  JR   C,digit   ; 30h-39h
0144   FE 11                  CP   11h   
0146   38 16                  JR   C,p3a   ; 3Ah-40h
0148   D6 11                  SUB   11h   ; A = c - 41h
014A   FE 1A                  CP   1Ah   
014C   38 69                  JR   C,upper   ; 41h-5Ah: A = letter index 0-25
014E   FE 20                  CP   20h   
0150   38 0A                  JR   C,p5b   ; 5Bh-60h
0152   FE 3A                  CP   3Ah   
0154   38 5B                  JR   C,lower   ; 61h-7Ah: A = 20h-39h (cell +64 bytes)
0156   FE 3E                  CP   3Eh   
0158                          IF   1-CHECKED   
0158   30 DA                  JR   NC,next0   ; 7Fh-FFh: ignored
015A                          ENDIF      
015A                          IF   CHECKED   
                              JR   Z,next0   ; 7Fh, DEL: ignored
                              JP   NC,e_hi   ; 80h-FFh: reserved
015A                          ENDIF      
015A   D6 1A                  SUB   1Ah   ; 7Bh-7Eh: -1Eh in all, index 28-31
015C   D6 09        P5B:      SUB   9   ; 5Bh-60h: -4 in all, index 22-27
015E   C6 05        P3A:      ADD   A,5   ; 3Ah-40h: index 15-21
0160                .macro PTABLE,
0160                             ; 
0160                 DB      h_store & 0FFh  ; !
0160                 DB      h_str & 0FFh    ; "
0160                 DB      h_num & 0FFh    ; #
0160                 DB      h_print & 0FFh  ; $
0160                 DB      h_swap & 0FFh   ; %
0160                 DB      h_and & 0FFh    ; &
0160                 DB      h_emit & 0FFh   ; '
0160                 DB      h_open & 0FFh   ; (
0160                 DB      h_close & 0FFh  ; )
0160                 DB      h_mul & 0FFh    ; *
0160                 DB      h_add & 0FFh    ; +
0160                 DB      h_cfetch & 0FFh ; ,
0160                 DB      h_sub & 0FFh    ; -
0160                 DB      h_cstore & 0FFh ; .
0160                 DB      h_div & 0FFh    ; /
0160                 DB      h_dup & 0FFh    ; :
0160                 DB      h_drop & 0FFh   ; ;
0160                 DB      h_lt & 0FFh     ; <
0160                 DB      h_eq & 0FFh     ; =
0160                 DB      h_gt & 0FFh     ; >
0160                 DB      h_key & 0FFh    ; ?
0160                 DB      h_fetch & 0FFh  ; @
0160                 DB      h_def & 0FFh    ; [
0160                 DB      h_break & 0FFh  ; \
0160                 DB      h_ret & 0FFh    ; ]
0160                 DB      h_xor & 0FFh    ; ^
0160                 DB      h_alloc & 0FFh  ; _
0160                 DB      h_grave & 0FFh  ; `
0160                 DB      h_tor & 0FFh    ; {
0160                 DB      h_or & 0FFh     ; |
0160                 DB      h_fromr & 0FFh  ; }
0160                 DB      h_not & 0FFh    ; ~
0160                .endm
0160                 
0160                             ; Punctuation: A = the PTAB index. The handler starts with HL = TOS,
0160                             ; untouched, and A, DE free.
0160   C6 3A        PUNCT:    ADD   A,PTAB & 0FFh   ; PTAB never crosses a page
0162   5F                     LD   E,A   
0163   16 04                  LD   D,PTAB / 256   ; (0 if the table is in page zero)
0165   FE 50                  CP   (PTAB & 0FFh) + NPG1   ; carry: one of the first NPG1
0167   1A                     LD   A,(DE)   
0168   5F                     LD   E,A   ; the handler's low byte
0169                          IF   (1-CPM)*(1-TABP0)   
                              LD   D,0   
0169                          ENDIF      
0169                          IFN   CPM   
                              RL   D   ; its page: 0 + carry
0169                          ENDIF      
0169                          IF   CPM   
0169   16 01                  LD   D,1   
016B   30 01                  JR   NC,pu1   
016D   14                     INC   D   ; its page: 1 + carry
016E                PU1:         
016E                          ENDIF      
016E   D5                     PUSH   DE   ; jump to it; the stack is balanced again
016F   C9                     RET      ;   when the handler starts
0170                             ; The rest of the startup: here so that the generic reset code can reach it
0170                             ; with JR. st0: find the program's NUL; the heap starts after it.
0170                             ; (The editor build has its own copy of this, next to the editor.)
0170                             ; A checked build first clears the lower half of the letter page (A = 0):
0170                             ; every variable starts at 0, every word cell holds 0000h, the address an
0170                             ; undefined word is caught at (see e_hi), and no key is held back.
0170                          IF   (1-CPM)*(1-EDITOR)*CHECKED   
                    INIT:     LD   HL,LET   
                    INI1:     LD   (HL),A   
                              INC   L   
                              JP   P,ini1   ; +00h to +7Fh
                              LD   BC,PROG   ; the IP
0170                          ENDIF      
0170                          IF   (1-CPM)*(1-EDITOR)   
                    ST0:      LD   H,B   
                              LD   L,C   
                              XOR   A   
                    ST1:      CP   (HL)   
                              INC   HL   
                              JR   NZ,st1   
0170                          ENDIF      
0170                          IF   1-EDITOR   
0170   22 7C 07     ST2:      LD   (HEAP),HL   
0173                          ENDIF      
0173                          IF   CHECKED*(1-EDITOR)   
                              RST   20h   ; minus the heap"s first address: "_' may not
                              LD   (NPEND),HL   ;   release below it
0173                          ENDIF      
0173                          IF   (1-CHECKED)*(1-EDITOR)*(1-CPM)   
                              LD   H,A   ; (A = 0) no key is held, and the break key
                              LD   L,A   ;   is on (the checked build has cleared
0173                          ENDIF      ;   these)
0173                          IF   (1-CHECKED)*(1-EDITOR)*CPM   
0173   21 00 00               LD   HL,0   
0176                          ENDIF      
0176                          IF   (1-CHECKED)*(1-EDITOR)   
0176   22 7A 07               LD   (KEYBUF),HL   
0179                          ENDIF      
0179                          IF   1-EDITOR   
0179   D9                     EXX      
017A   21 E0 05               LD   HL,RSTOP   ; the return stack is empty
017D   D9                     EXX      
017E   F7                     RST   30h   ; (its return address is thrown away)
017F                          ENDIF      
017F                             ; In the unchecked generic editor build the table is here, in the first
017F                             ; page, which saves loading D twice. (The other builds have no room for it
017F                             ; here: theirs is further down.)
017F                          IF   TABP0   
                    PTAB:        
                              ;*Macro unroll:  PTABLE
                              DB   h_store & 0FFh   
                              DB   h_str & 0FFh   
                              DB   h_num & 0FFh   
                              DB   h_print & 0FFh   
                              DB   h_swap & 0FFh   
                              DB   h_and & 0FFh   
                              DB   h_emit & 0FFh   
                              DB   h_open & 0FFh   
                              DB   h_close & 0FFh   
                              DB   h_mul & 0FFh   
                              DB   h_add & 0FFh   
                              DB   h_cfetch & 0FFh   
                              DB   h_sub & 0FFh   
                              DB   h_cstore & 0FFh   
                              DB   h_div & 0FFh   
                              DB   h_dup & 0FFh   
                              DB   h_drop & 0FFh   
                              DB   h_lt & 0FFh   
                              DB   h_eq & 0FFh   
                              DB   h_gt & 0FFh   
                              DB   h_key & 0FFh   
                              DB   h_fetch & 0FFh   
                              DB   h_def & 0FFh   
                              DB   h_break & 0FFh   
                              DB   h_ret & 0FFh   
                              DB   h_xor & 0FFh   
                              DB   h_alloc & 0FFh   
                              DB   h_grave & 0FFh   
                              DB   h_tor & 0FFh   
                              DB   h_or & 0FFh   
                              DB   h_fromr & 0FFh   
                              DB   h_not & 0FFh   
                    PTABEND:      
017F                          ENDIF      
017F                             ; =============================================================================
017F                             ;  Handlers that must start in the image's first page: ^ _ ` | ~
017F                             ;  (00bbIGFuZCA= are up among the RST routines.) The machine-code call, exec,
017F                             ;  is here too: it belongs to "`" and makes the page come out right.
017F                             ; =============================================================================
017F   D1           H_XOR:    POP   DE   
0180   7C                     LD   A,H   
0181   AA                     XOR   D   
0182   67                     LD   H,A   
0183   7D                     LD   A,L   
0184   AB                     XOR   E   
0185   6F                     LD   L,A   
0186   F7                     RST   30h   
0187   D1           H_OR:     POP   DE   
0188   7C                     LD   A,H   
0189   B2                     OR   D   
018A   67                     LD   H,A   
018B   7D                     LD   A,L   
018C   B3                     OR   E   
018D   6F                     LD   L,A   
018E   F7                     RST   30h   
018F   E7           H_NOT:    RST   20h   ; ~x = -x - 1
0190   2B                     DEC   HL   
0191   F7                     RST   30h   
0192                             ; "_" ( n -- addr ): the heap pointer moves by n, a signed count (the add is
0192                             ; the same either way); TOS is the old pointer.
0192   ED 5B 7C 07  H_ALLOC:   LD   DE,(HEAP)   
0196                          IF   CHECKED*CPM   
                              LD   A,H   ; the count's sign, for chkhp
0196                          ENDIF      
0196   19                     ADD   HL,DE   ; the new top
0197                          IF   CHECKED   
                              CALL   chkhp   
0197                          ENDIF      
0197   22 7C 07               LD   (HEAP),HL   
019A   EB                     EX   DE,HL   
019B   F7                     RST   30h   
019C   D9           EXEC:     EXX      
019D   22 34 07               LD   (RSAVE),HL   ; machine code may change the alternates
01A0   D9                     EXX      
01A1   CD 2B 01               CALL   jphl   
01A4   D9                     EXX      
01A5   2A 34 07               LD   HL,(RSAVE)   
01A8   D9                     EXX      
01A9   E1                     POP   HL   
01AA   F7                     RST   30h   
01AB                             ; ---- the letters and digits (here, in the middle, so that the inner loop's
01AB                             ; ---- short jumps reach them, and the handlers after them reach rpushn) ------
01AB                             ; Digits: step back onto the first digit and read the whole number.
01AB   E5           DIGIT:    PUSH   HL   
01AC   0B                     DEC   BC   
01AD   CD 24 03               CALL   rdnum   
01B0   F7                     RST   30h   
01B1                             ; a-z: push the cell's address (the cell is the variable)
01B1   E5           LOWER:    PUSH   HL   
01B2   87                     ADD   A,A   
01B3   6F                     LD   L,A   
01B4   26 07                  LD   H,LETPAGE   
01B6   F7                     RST   30h   
01B7                             ; A-Z: call the word. The return address (the IP after the letter) goes on
01B7                             ; the return stack, and the IP becomes the address in the letter's cell.
01B7   C5           UPPER:    PUSH   BC   ; the return address, for rpushn
01B8   EB                     EX   DE,HL   ; park TOS
01B9   87                     ADD   A,A   
01BA   6F                     LD   L,A   
01BB   26 07                  LD   H,LETPAGE   ; HL -> cell
01BD   4E                     LD   C,(HL)   
01BE   2C                     INC   L   
01BF   46                     LD   B,(HL)   ; IP = the word's body
01C0   EB                     EX   DE,HL   ; TOS back, and fall into rpushn
01C1                             ; rpushn: move the top cell of the data stack (in memory) to the return
01C1                             ; stack, then next. Everything that pushes the return stack ends here.
01C1                             ; 
01C1                             ; The break key is looked at here, so at every word call and loop-back (and
01C1                             ; block entry and "{"), but only one time in 256: B', which nothing else
01C1                             ; uses, counts them. Reading the keyboard can be slow (it is a BDOS call
01C1                             ; under CP/M), and this way it costs a loop four bytes and 14 T-states.
01C1                             ; (DEC B, not DJNZ: its zero flag lasts through the EXX, so one EXX serves
01C1                             ; both ways out.)
01C1   D9           RPUSHN:   EXX      
01C2   D1                     POP   DE   
01C3   2B                     DEC   HL   
01C4   72                     LD   (HL),D   
01C5   2B                     DEC   HL   
01C6   73                     LD   (HL),E   
01C7   05                     DEC   B   
01C8   D9                     EXX      
01C9   CC 6C 04               CALL   Z,pollk   
01CC   F7                     RST   30h   
01CD                             ; ---- the grave -------------------------------------------------------------
01CD                             ; The grave is a prefix: with the character after it, it is one command.
01CD                             ; The characters are tested one after another, each SUB taking off the step
01CD                             ; from the one before, so A is 0 (and the carry clear) when a handler is
01CD                             ; reached. Two are here, where they keep the first page as full as the
01CD                             ; layout needs; grave2 has the rest.
01CD                             ; 
01CD                             ;   `!  ( addr -- )  calls the machine code at TOS. The code is entered by
01CD                             ;       CALL with the data stack above the return address; it must keep BC,
01CD                             ;       and on return the top cell becomes the new TOS.
01CD                             ;   `'  ( -- )  new line: CR LF
01CD   0A           H_GRAVE:   LD   A,(BC)   
01CE   03                     INC   BC   
01CF   D6 21                  SUB   "!"   
01D1   28 C9                  JR   Z,exec   
01D3   D6 06                  SUB   27h-"!"   ; "'"
01D5   C2 81 03               JP   NZ,grave2   
01D8   3E 0D                  LD   A,13   
01DA   EF                     RST   28h   
01DB   3E 0A                  LD   A,10   
01DD   EF                     RST   28h   
01DE   F7                     RST   30h   
01DF                             ; ---- where the two pages meet ----------------------------------------------
01DF                             ; The first page ends somewhere among the next four handlers, ] \ [ @ (they
01DF                             ; are in falling code order for this), and where exactly differs between the
01DF                             ; builds: NPG1 follows. Every handler below these four must start in the
01DF                             ; second page, and every one above in the first; chktab.py checks both.
01DF                             ; "]" returns: pop an address and jump to it.
01DF   CF           H_RET:    RST   08h   
01E0   42                     LD   B,D   
01E1   4B                     LD   C,E   
01E2   F7           BRK1:     RST   30h   
01E3                             ; "\" ( flag -- ): true skips to the next ")" or "]" at this level; ")"
01E3                             ; drops the block start, "]" returns. No closer at all ends the program.
01E3   7C           H_BREAK:   LD   A,H   
01E4   B5                     OR   L   
01E5   E1                     POP   HL   
01E6   28 FA                  JR   Z,brk1   
01E8   CD 46 03               CALL   skip   
01EB   B7                     OR   A   ; skip returns 0 for ")"
01EC   20 F1                  JR   NZ,h_ret   
01EE   CF           RDROP:    RST   08h   
01EF   F7                     RST   30h   
01F0                             ; "[" followed by a letter stores the body"s address in that letter"s cell:
01F0                             ; uppercase is a word, lowercase a variable. Followed by a space it pushes
01F0                             ; the body"s address instead. Either way it then skips to the matching "]'.
01F0                             ; (The unchecked build takes anything that is not a letter as the space; the
01F0                             ; checked build stops on it.)
01F0   0A           H_DEF:    LD   A,(BC)   
01F1   03                     INC   BC   
01F2   D6 41                  SUB   "A"   ; a letter gives 0-25 or 32-57: lowercase
01F4   5F                     LD   E,A   ;   lands 64 bytes up
01F5   E6 DF                  AND   0DFh   ; fold case
01F7   FE 1A                  CP   26   
01F9   30 0B                  JR   NC,def2   ; not a letter
01FB   CB 23                  SLA   E   
01FD   16 07                  LD   D,LETPAGE   ; DE -> cell
01FF   79                     LD   A,C   
0200   12                     LD   (DE),A   
0201   1C                     INC   E   
0202   78                     LD   A,B   
0203   12                     LD   (DE),A   
0204   18 03                  JR   skipnx   
0206                DEF2:        
0206                          IF   CHECKED   
                              LD   A,E   
                              CP   " "-"A"+256   
                              JP   NZ,e_brack   ; anything but a letter or a space
0206                          ENDIF      
0206   E5                     PUSH   HL   ; an anonymous block: push its address
0207   60                     LD   H,B   
0208   69                     LD   L,C   
0209                SKIPNX:      
0209                          IF   CHECKED   
                              DEC   BC   ; back onto the letter, so that skip finds its
0209                          ENDIF      ;   opener, the "[", just before where it starts
0209   CD 46 03     SKIPO:    CALL   skip   
020C   F7                     RST   30h   
020D   5E           H_FETCH:   LD   E,(HL)   ; "@"
020E   23                     INC   HL   
020F   56                     LD   D,(HL)   
0210   EB                     EX   DE,HL   
0211   F7                     RST   30h   
0212                             ; =============================================================================
0212                             ;  Handlers that must start in the image's second page.
0212                             ;  "?" is the last (with "," inside it), so its long tail may run past that
0212                             ;  page.
0212                             ; =============================================================================
0212                             ; "(" ( flag -- ): true pushes the block start and enters; false skips to
0212                             ; the matching ")".
0212   7C           H_OPEN:   LD   A,H   
0213   B5                     OR   L   
0214   E1                     POP   HL   
0215   28 F2                  JR   Z,skipo   
0217   C5                     PUSH   BC   ; the block starts at the IP
0218   18 A7                  JR   rpushn   
021A                             ; ")" ( flag -- ): true jumps back to the block start (and keeps it); false
021A                             ; drops it and carries on.
021A   7C           H_CLOSE:   LD   A,H   
021B   B5                     OR   L   
021C   E1                     POP   HL   
021D   28 CF                  JR   Z,rdrop   
021F   CF                     RST   08h   ; pop the block start ...
0220   42                     LD   B,D   
0221   4B                     LD   C,E   
0222   C5                     PUSH   BC   
0223   18 9C                  JR   rpushn   ; ... and push it back
0225                             ; ---- arithmetic and logic: ( NOS TOS -- result ) ---------------------------
0225                             ; "-" has two jobs: directly before a digit it starts a negative number.
0225   0A           H_SUB:    LD   A,(BC)   
0226   D6 30                  SUB   "0"   
0228   FE 0A                  CP   10   
022A   38 04                  JR   C,negnum   
022C   E7                     RST   20h   ; a - b = a + (-b): fall into "+"
022D   D1           H_ADD:    POP   DE   
022E   19                     ADD   HL,DE   
022F   F7                     RST   30h   
0230   E5           NEGNUM:   PUSH   HL   ; a negative number: read it, negate it
0231   CD 24 03               CALL   rdnum   
0234   E7                     RST   20h   
0235   F7                     RST   30h   
0236   D1           H_AND:    POP   DE   
0237   7C                     LD   A,H   
0238   A2                     AND   D   
0239   67                     LD   H,A   
023A   7D                     LD   A,L   
023B   A3                     AND   E   
023C   6F                     LD   L,A   
023D   F7                     RST   30h   
023E                             ; Signed compares. Both are "HL < DE" for the right pair: "<" swaps the two
023E                             ; cells first. Flipping both sign bits turns a signed compare into an
023E                             ; unsigned one (and XOR clears the carry for SBC); SBC HL,HL then turns the
023E                             ; carry into -1 or 0 with no branch.
023E   E3           H_LT:     EX   (SP),HL   ; a < b: HL = a, and b is popped next
023F   D1           H_GT:     POP   DE   ; a > b  is  b < a: HL = b, DE = a
0240   7C                     LD   A,H   
0241   EE 80                  XOR   80h   
0243   67                     LD   H,A   
0244   7A                     LD   A,D   
0245   EE 80                  XOR   80h   
0247   57                     LD   D,A   
0248   ED 52                  SBC   HL,DE   ; carry if HL < DE
024A   ED 62        TF:       SBC   HL,HL   ; carry -> -1 or 0
024C   F7                     RST   30h   
024D   D1           H_EQ:     POP   DE   
024E   B7                     OR   A   
024F   ED 52                  SBC   HL,DE   
0251   7C                     LD   A,H   
0252   B5                     OR   L   
0253   FE 01                  CP   1   ; carry only if a - b = 0
0255   18 F3                  JR   tf   
0257                             ; "*": shift-and-add, 16 rounds; only the low 16 bits are kept. The
0257                             ; multiplier shifts up through A:C.
0257   D1           H_MUL:    POP   DE   ; DE = multiplicand
0258   C5                     PUSH   BC   
0259   7C                     LD   A,H   
025A   4D                     LD   C,L   ; A:C = multiplier
025B   21 00 00               LD   HL,0   
025E   06 10                  LD   B,16   
0260   29           MUL1:     ADD   HL,HL   
0261   CB 21                  SLA   C   
0263   17                     RLA      
0264   30 01                  JR   NC,mul2   
0266   19                     ADD   HL,DE   
0267   10 F7        MUL2:     DJNZ   mul1   
0269   C1                     POP   BC   
026A   F7                     RST   30h   
026B                             ; "/" ( a b -- q r ): the remainder is on top. Truncates toward zero; r takes
026B                             ; a's sign. Divide |a| by |b|, then q gets the sign of a XOR b and r the sign
026B                             ; of a. Dividing by zero returns two cells of no meaning; the checked build
026B                             ; stops on it.
026B                H_DIV:       
026B                          IF   CHECKED   
                              LD   A,H   
                              OR   L   
                              JP   Z,e_zero   
026B                          ENDIF      
026B   D1                     POP   DE   ; DE = a, HL = b
026C   C5                     PUSH   BC   ; free BC for udiv
026D   D5                     PUSH   DE   ; a, for r's sign
026E   7A                     LD   A,D   
026F   AC                     XOR   H   
0270   F5                     PUSH   AF   ; S flag = sign of q
0271   CB 7C                  BIT   7,H   
0273   C4 20 01               CALL   NZ,neg16   ; HL = |b|
0276   EB                     EX   DE,HL   
0277   CB 7C                  BIT   7,H   
0279   C4 20 01               CALL   NZ,neg16   ; HL = |a|, DE = |b|
027C   CD FE 02               CALL   udiv   ; HL = q, DE = r
027F   F1                     POP   AF   
0280   FC 20 01               CALL   M,neg16   ; q's sign
0283   EB                     EX   DE,HL   ; HL = r, DE = q
0284   F1                     POP   AF   ; A = a's high byte
0285   B7                     OR   A   
0286   FC 20 01               CALL   M,neg16   ; r's sign
0289   C1                     POP   BC   
028A   D5                     PUSH   DE   ; q under r
028B   F7                     RST   30h   
028C                             ; ---- stack and storage -----------------------------------------------------
028C   E5           H_DUP:    PUSH   HL   ; ":"
028D   F7                     RST   30h   
028E   E3           H_SWAP:   EX   (SP),HL   ; "%"
028F   F7                     RST   30h   
0290                             ; (The checked build tests the address before it takes the value off the
0290                             ; stack, so that an error report shows both.)
0290                H_CSTORE:      ; "." ( c addr -- )
0290                          IF   CHECKED   
                              CALL   chkst   
0290                          ENDIF      
0290   D1                     POP   DE   
0291   73                     LD   (HL),E   
0292   DF           H_DROP:   RST   18h   ; ";" is this one byte
0293                H_STORE:      ; "!" ( n addr -- )
0293                          IF   CHECKED   
                              CALL   chkst   
0293                          ENDIF      
0293   D1                     POP   DE   
0294   73                     LD   (HL),E   
0295   23                     INC   HL   
0296   72                     LD   (HL),D   
0297   DF                     RST   18h   
0298                             ; ---- console ---------------------------------------------------------------
0298                             ; 22h pushes the address of the text after it and skips the string.
0298   E5           H_STR:    PUSH   HL   
0299   60                     LD   H,B   
029A   69                     LD   L,C   
029B   CD 3B 03               CALL   skipstr   
029E                          IF   CHECKED   
                              OR   A   ; 0: the text ran out before the closing quote
                              JP   Z,e_quote   
029E                          ENDIF      
029E   F7                     RST   30h   
029F                             ; "$" prints the string at TOS, decoding escapes: "/" plus a character
029F                             ; clears that character"s bit 6 (/M is CR, /` is space; "/" and ""' have no
029F                             ; bit 6, so // and /" give themselves).
029F                          IF   1-CHECKED   
029F   7E           H_PRINT:   LD   A,(HL)   
02A0   23                     INC   HL   
02A1   FE 22                  CP   22h   
02A3   28 0D                  JR   Z,pr9   
02A5   FE 2F                  CP   "/"   
02A7   20 04                  JR   NZ,pr1   
02A9   7E                     LD   A,(HL)   
02AA   23                     INC   HL   
02AB   E6 BF                  AND   0BFh   
02AD   EF           PR1:      RST   28h   
02AE   18 EF                  JR   h_print   
02B0                          ENDIF      
02B0                          IF   CHECKED   
                                 ; (The checked build has the loop as a routine, prstr, which the error
                                 ; report uses too. The address is kept on the stack meanwhile: a report
                                 ; shows the stack as it was before the "$".)
                    H_PRINT:   PUSH   HL   
                              CALL   prstr   
                              POP   DE   
                              RST   18h   
02B0                          ENDIF      
02B0   7D           H_EMIT:   LD   A,L   ; "'"
02B1   EF                     RST   28h   
02B2   DF           PR9:      RST   18h   
02B3                             ; "#" prints TOS as a signed decimal number, with no space after it.
02B3   C5           H_NUM:    PUSH   BC   
02B4   CD 67 03               CALL   psgn   
02B7   C1                     POP   BC   
02B8   DF                     RST   18h   
02B9                             ; "?" ( n -- c ) or ( -n -- addr )
02B9                             ;   n > 0: wait about n ms for a key; 0 if none came
02B9                             ;   n = 0: wait for a key
02B9                             ;          (both stir the random seed while they wait: see kt2)
02B9                             ;   n < 0: read a line of at most -n characters, with echo. The buffer
02B9                             ;          holds 127 characters and the CR: a bigger count is taken as 127.
02B9   CB 7C        H_KEY:    BIT   7,H   
02BB   20 22                  JR   NZ,line   
02BD   1E 28        KT1:      LD   E,MSLOOP   ; one millisecond, roughly
02BF   CD 9A 04     KT2:      CALL   getk   
02C2   20 17                  JR   NZ,kt3   
02C4   1D                     DEC   E   
02C5   20 F8                  JR   NZ,kt2   
02C7   EB                     EX   DE,HL   ; a millisecond with no key stirs the random
02C8   2A 76 07               LD   HL,(SEED)   ;   seed by one: how long a key takes to come
02CB   23                     INC   HL   ;   is the one thing here that is not the
02CC   22 76 07               LD   (SEED),HL   ;   same every time
02CF   EB                     EX   DE,HL   
02D0   7C                     LD   A,H   ; 0? never counts down: it waits
02D1   B5                     OR   L   
02D2   28 E9                  JR   Z,kt1   
02D4   2B                     DEC   HL   
02D5   7C                     LD   A,H   
02D6   B5                     OR   L   
02D7   20 E4                  JR   NZ,kt1   ; A = 0 if the time ran out
02D9   FE                     DB   0FEh   ; (CP n: steps over the one byte of ",")
02DA   7E           H_CFETCH:   LD   A,(HL)   ; "," shares "?"s ending: A becomes TOS
02DB   6F           KT3:      LD   L,A   
02DC   26 00                  LD   H,0   
02DE   F7                     RST   30h   
02DF                          IF   CPM   
02DF                             ; CP/M: BDOS 10 does the editing (the spec allows the platform's
02DF                             ; own line editor). It doesn't store the CR, so it is added here.
02DF   11 7F 00     LINE:     LD   DE,127   ; TOS is minus the count: adding 127 carries
02E2   19                     ADD   HL,DE   ;   only for 1 to 127, and leaves 127 - count
02E3   9F                     SBC   A,A   
02E4   A5                     AND   L   ; (0 for a count that is too big)
02E5   EE 7F                  XOR   127   ; A = the count, 127 at most
02E7   32 7E 07               LD   (LBHDR),A   
02EA   11 7E 07               LD   DE,LBHDR   
02ED   3E 0A                  LD   A,10   
02EF   CD B8 04               CALL   bdosx   
02F2   21 7F 07               LD   HL,LBHDR+1   
02F5   7E                     LD   A,(HL)   ; the count typed (0-127)
02F6   2C                     INC   L   ; HL = LINEBUF, whose low byte is 80h:
02F7   85                     ADD   A,L   ;   adding the count to L can't carry
02F8   6F                     LD   L,A   
02F9   36 0D                  LD   (HL),13   
02FB                          ENDIF      
02FB                          IFN   CPM   
                                 ; Generic: Backspace takes the last character back (and is echoed as
                                 ; it is), CR ends (stored, not echoed), every other key is stored and
                                 ; echoed until the line is full. The line buffer starts at offset 80h
                                 ; of its page, so L alone is the place in the line: D holds the L of
                                 ; a full line.
                    LINE:     LD   DE,127   ; TOS is minus the count: adding 127 carries
                              ADD   HL,DE   ;   only for 1 to 127, and leaves 127 - count
                              SBC   A,A   
                              AND   L   ; (0 for a count that is too big)
                              CPL      
                              LD   D,A   ; D = the L of a full line: 80h + count, FFh
                                 ;   at most
                              LD   HL,LINEBUF   
                    LN2:      CALL   getk   
                              JR   Z,ln2   
                              CP   13   
                              JR   Z,ln5   
                              CP   8   
                              JR   Z,ln4   
                              LD   E,A   
                              LD   A,L   
                              CP   D   
                              JR   Z,ln2   ; full
                              LD   (HL),E   
                              INC   L   
                              LD   A,E   
                    LN3:      RST   28h   
                              JR   ln2   
                    LN4:      DEC   L   ; Backspace: one back, and echo it,
                              JP   M,ln3   ;   unless the line was empty (L left the
                              INC   L   ;   upper half of the page)
                              JR   ln2   
                    LN5:      LD   (HL),A   ; the CR
02FB                          ENDIF      
02FB   2E 80                  LD   L,LINEBUF & 0FFh   
02FD   F7                     RST   30h   
02FE                             ; =============================================================================
02FE                             ;  More routines (no handler starts past this point)
02FE                             ; =============================================================================
02FE                             ; udiv: unsigned HL / DE (DE <= 8000h). Returns HL = quotient, DE = remainder.
02FE                             ; Uses A, BC; the caller saves the IP. The dividend shifts up through A:C
02FE                             ; while the quotient bits arrive at the bottom of C.
02FE                             ; Dividing by 2 is one shift (the spec wants that fast).
02FE   7B           UDIV:     LD   A,E   
02FF   EE 02                  XOR   2   
0301   B2                     OR   D   
0302   20 07                  JR   NZ,udv0   
0304   CB 3C                  SRL   H   
0306   CB 1D                  RR   L   ; the quotient
0308   8F                     ADC   A,A   
0309   5F                     LD   E,A   ; the remainder: the bit that fell out (D is 0)
030A   C9                     RET      
030B   7C           UDV0:     LD   A,H   
030C   4D                     LD   C,L   
030D   21 00 00               LD   HL,0   
0310   06 10                  LD   B,16   
0312   CB 21        UDV1:     SLA   C   
0314   17                     RLA      
0315   ED 6A                  ADC   HL,HL   
0317   ED 52                  SBC   HL,DE   ; carry is clear here: the remainder
0319   30 02                  JR   NC,udv2   ;   always fits in 16 bits
031B   19                     ADD   HL,DE   ; too much: put it back, and cancel the
031C   0D                     DEC   C   ;   INC below
031D   0C           UDV2:     INC   C   ; a quotient bit
031E   10 F2                  DJNZ   udv1   
0320   EB                     EX   DE,HL   ; DE = remainder
0321   67                     LD   H,A   
0322   69                     LD   L,C   ; HL = quotient
0323   C9                     RET      
0324                             ; rdnum: read decimal digits at IP into HL; IP is left on the first
0324                             ; non-digit. Values wrap at 16 bits, as the spec says.
0324   21 00 00     RDNUM:    LD   HL,0   
0327   0A           RDN1:     LD   A,(BC)   
0328   D6 30                  SUB   "0"   
032A   FE 0A                  CP   10   
032C   D0                     RET   NC   
032D   03                     INC   BC   
032E   54                     LD   D,H   
032F   5D                     LD   E,L   
0330   29                     ADD   HL,HL   
0331   29                     ADD   HL,HL   
0332   19                     ADD   HL,DE   
0333   29                     ADD   HL,HL   ; HL * 10
0334   5F                     LD   E,A   
0335   16 00                  LD   D,0   
0337   19                     ADD   HL,DE   
0338   18 ED                  JR   rdn1   
033A                             ; skipstr: IP is inside a string; step past its closing quote. "/" escapes
033A                             ; the next character, so "/"" does not end it. Leaves A = 22h.
033A                          IF   1-CHECKED   
033A   03           SS0:      INC   BC   
033B   0A           SKIPSTR:   LD   A,(BC)   
033C   03                     INC   BC   
033D   FE 2F                  CP   "/"   
033F   28 F9                  JR   Z,ss0   
0341   FE 22                  CP   22h   
0343   20 F6                  JR   NZ,skipstr   
0345   C9                     RET      
0346                          ENDIF      
0346                          IF   CHECKED   
                                 ; The checked build never steps over a NUL: if the text runs out first it
                                 ; returns A = 0 with the IP on the NUL.
                    SKIPSTR:   LD   A,(BC)   
                              OR   A   
                              RET   Z   
                              INC   BC   
                              CP   22h   
                              RET   Z   
                              CP   "/"   
                              JR   NZ,skipstr   
                              LD   A,(BC)   ; the escaped character
                              OR   A   
                              RET   Z   
                              INC   BC   
                              JR   skipstr   
0346                          ENDIF      
0346                             ; skip: read past text to the closer at this level, and return A = 0 if it
0346                             ; was ")" and 2 if it was "]". Brackets of both kinds count together;
0346                             ; strings are stepped over whole. A NUL first ends the program (for "\" with
0346                             ; no closer; anything else that runs into the NUL had unbalanced brackets
0346                             ; anyway). D counts the open levels, starting at 1 for the one we are in:
0346                             ; skip sets it to 0 and falls through the INC that an opener comes back to.
0346                             ; 
0346                             ; The checked build also looks at the character the skip was started by,
0346                             ; which is always the one just before where it starts: "(" must end at ")",
0346                             ; "[" at "]", and neither may run into the NUL (N); a string with no closing
0346                             ; quote counts as running into it. "\" takes either closer. IX keeps the
0346                             ; place where the skip started, for the report.
0346                SKIP:        
0346                          IF   CHECKED   
                              PUSH   BC   
                              POP   IX   
                              DEC   BC   
                              LD   A,(BC)   
                              INC   BC   
                              LD   E,A   ; E = the opener: ( [ or \
0346                          ENDIF      
0346   16 00                  LD   D,0   
0348   14           SK3:      INC   D   ; an opener: one deeper
0349   0A           SK1:      LD   A,(BC)   
034A                          IF   1-CHECKED   
034A   03                     INC   BC   
034B   B7                     OR   A   
034C   CA 00 00               JP   Z,SKEND   ; (the end of the program)
034F                          ENDIF      
034F                          IF   CHECKED   
                              OR   A   
                              JR   Z,sk6   ; (the IP stays on the NUL)
                              INC   BC   
034F                          ENDIF      
034F   FE 22                  CP   22h   
0351   CC 3B 03               CALL   Z,skipstr   ; leaves A = 22h, which matches nothing below
0354   D6 28                  SUB   "("   ;   (or 0, and then the NUL is read next)
0356   28 F0                  JR   Z,sk3   
0358   3D                     DEC   A   ; ")"
0359   28 08                  JR   Z,sk4   
035B   D6 32                  SUB   "["-")"   
035D   28 E9                  JR   Z,sk3   
035F   FE 02                  CP   "]"-"["   
0361   20 E6                  JR   NZ,sk1   
0363   15           SK4:      DEC   D   
0364                          IF   1-CHECKED   
0364   C8                     RET   Z   ; the closer at this level
0365   18 E2                  JR   sk1   
0367                          ENDIF      
0367                          IF   CHECKED   
                              JR   NZ,sk1   
                              LD   D,A   ; the closer at this level: 0 or 2. Bit 1 of the
                              XOR   E   ;   opener is 0 for "(" and 1 for "[", and only
                              AND   6   ;   "\" has bit 2: so this is 2 for the wrong
                              CP   2   ;   closer, and only then
                              LD   A,D   
                              RET   NZ   
                              JR   sk7   
                    SK6:      BIT   2,E   ; the text ran out:
                              JP   NZ,SKEND   ;   "\" with no closer ends the program
                    SK7:      PUSH   IX   ; N. The place is the opener
                              POP   BC   
                              LD   A,"N"   
                              JP   errp   ; (errp drops skip's return address)
0367                          ENDIF      
0367                             ; psgn: print HL as a signed number. Uses BC.
0367   CB 7C        PSGN:     BIT   7,H   
0369   28 04                  JR   Z,pdec   
036B   3E 2D                  LD   A,"-"   
036D   EF                     RST   28h   
036E   E7                     RST   20h   
036F                             ; pdec: print HL unsigned, by recursion on HL / 10 (the stack holds digits).
036F                             ; Uses BC.
036F   11 0A 00     PDEC:     LD   DE,10   
0372   CD FE 02               CALL   udiv   ; HL = HL / 10, E = the last digit
0375   7B                     LD   A,E   
0376   F5                     PUSH   AF   
0377   7C                     LD   A,H   
0378   B5                     OR   L   
0379   C4 6F 03               CALL   NZ,pdec   
037C   F1                     POP   AF   
037D   C6 30                  ADD   A,"0"   
037F   EF                     RST   28h   
0380   C9                     RET      
0381                             ; =============================================================================
0381                             ;  The grave's other codes. h_grave comes here with A = the character minus
0381                             ;  27h, not zero; the tests carry on from there. The four characters from
0381                             ;  "+" to "." follow one another, so one range test finds them and two
0381                             ;  rotates tell them apart.
0381                             ; 
0381                             ;    `$  ( addr -- addr' )  the hex loader: pairs of hex digits are stored
0381                             ;        from addr until a non-hex character; then a RET (C9h) is written
0381                             ;        and its address is left. An odd last digit is consumed and dropped.
0381                             ;    `+  ( addr -- n )   add 1 to the cell at addr and leave its new value
0381                             ;    `,  ( n -- r )      a random number from 0 to n-1 (n is 1 to 32767)
0381                             ;    `-  ( addr -- n )   subtract 1 from the cell at addr, the same way
0381                             ;    `.  ( -- addr )     the address of the random seed
0381                             ;    `<  ( a b -- n )    the smaller of the two (signed)
0381                             ;    `>  ( a b -- n )    the larger
0381                             ;    `?  ( flag -- )     the cursor off (0) or on
0381                             ;    `@  ( row col -- )  the cursor to that row and column, both from 0
0381                             ;    `^  ( -- )          clear the screen and home the cursor
0381                             ;    `_  ( -- )          clear from the cursor to the end of the line
0381                             ; 
0381                             ;  Any other character is unsafe: the unchecked build takes it as "_", the
0381                             ;  checked build stops with W.
0381                             ; =============================================================================
0381   D6 04        GRAVE2:   SUB   "+"-27h   ; "+" "," "-" "." leave 0 to 3
0383   FE 04                  CP   4   
0385   30 32                  JR   NC,gv2   
0387   1F                     RRA      ; carry: "," or "."; bit 0 of A: "-" or "."
0388   38 0E                  JR   C,gv3   
038A                             ; `+ and `-: one routine.
038A                          IF   CHECKED   
                              LD   D,A   ; (the checked build tests the address first,
                              CALL   chkst   ;   as "!" does: the test uses A, and under
                              LD   A,D   ;   CP/M E too)
038A                          ENDIF      
038A   5E                     LD   E,(HL)   
038B   23                     INC   HL   
038C   56                     LD   D,(HL)   
038D   1F                     RRA      ; carry: "-"
038E   38 02                  JR   C,gi1   
0390   13                     INC   DE   
0391   13                     INC   DE   
0392   1B           GI1:      DEC   DE   
0393   72                     LD   (HL),D   
0394   2B                     DEC   HL   
0395   73                     LD   (HL),E   
0396   EB                     EX   DE,HL   ; the new value is TOS
0397   F7                     RST   30h   
0398   1F           GV3:      RRA      ; carry: "."
0399   38 19                  JR   C,g_seed   
039B                             ; `, ( n -- r ). The seed goes one step on: seed * 261 + 1, which takes
039B                             ; every 16-bit value in turn. The high bits of such a seed are the good ones
039B                             ; and the low ones repeat soon, so the high byte is folded into the low
039B                             ; (XOR) before the remainder of dividing by n is taken.
039B                             ; n must be 1 to 32767: the checked build stops with Z on anything less
039B                             ; than 1.
039B                G_RND:       
039B                          IF   CHECKED   
                              DEC   HL   
                              BIT   7,H   ; n - 1 negative: n is 0 or less
                              INC   HL   
                              JP   NZ,e_zero   
039B                          ENDIF      
039B   EB                     EX   DE,HL   ; DE = n
039C   C5                     PUSH   BC   
039D   2A 76 07               LD   HL,(SEED)   
03A0   44                     LD   B,H   
03A1   4D                     LD   C,L   
03A2   29                     ADD   HL,HL   
03A3   29                     ADD   HL,HL   
03A4   09                     ADD   HL,BC   ; * 5
03A5   23                     INC   HL   ; + 1
03A6   7C                     LD   A,H   
03A7   81                     ADD   A,C   
03A8   67                     LD   H,A   ; + * 256: * 261 + 1
03A9   22 76 07               LD   (SEED),HL   
03AC   AD                     XOR   L   ; (A is still the high byte)
03AD   6F                     LD   L,A   
03AE   CD FE 02               CALL   udiv   ; DE = the remainder
03B1   EB                     EX   DE,HL   
03B2   C1                     POP   BC   
03B3   F7                     RST   30h   
03B4                             ; `. pushes the address of the random seed.
03B4   E5           G_SEED:   PUSH   HL   
03B5   21 76 07               LD   HL,SEED   
03B8   F7                     RST   30h   
03B9   C6 07        GV2:      ADD   A,"+"-"$"   ; "$"
03BB   20 13                  JR   NZ,gv4   
03BD   CD 5A 04     HX1:      CALL   hexc   
03C0   30 0B                  JR   NC,hx2   
03C2   77                     LD   (HL),A   ; the high digit goes in first ...
03C3   CD 5A 04               CALL   hexc   
03C6   30 05                  JR   NC,hx2   ; odd digit: consumed, and the RET below
03C8   ED 6F                  RLD      ;   overwrites it
03CA   23                     INC   HL   ; ... and RLD shifts it up under the low one
03CB   18 F0                  JR   hx1   
03CD   36 C9        HX2:      LD   (HL),0C9h   ; (never range-checked: the spec says so)
03CF   F7                     RST   30h   
03D0   D6 18        GV4:      SUB   "<"-"$"   
03D2   28 1F                  JR   Z,g_min   
03D4   D6 02                  SUB   ">"-"<"   
03D6   28 1A                  JR   Z,g_max   
03D8   3D                     DEC   A   ; "?"
03D9   28 2A                  JR   Z,g_cur   
03DB   3D                     DEC   A   ; "@"
03DC   28 3D                  JR   Z,g_at   
03DE   D6 1E                  SUB   "^"-"@"   ; "^" leaves 0 and "_" leaves 1
03E0                          IF   CHECKED   
                              CP   2   
                              JP   NC,e_brack   ; anything else: W. The place is the character
                              OR   A   
03E0                          ENDIF      
03E0                          IF   ANSI   
03E0   20 07                  JR   NZ,ge1   
03E2   CD 33 04               CALL   csi   ; "^": ESC [ H homes the cursor, and then
03E5   3E 48                  LD   A,"H"   ;   ESC [ J clears from there to the end of
03E7   EF                     RST   28h   ;   the screen
03E8   AF                     XOR   A   
03E9   C6 4A        GE1:      ADD   A,"J"   ; "_": ESC [ K clears to the end of the line
03EB   5F                     LD   E,A   
03EC   CD 33 04               CALL   csi   
03EF   7B                     LD   A,E   
03F0   EF                     RST   28h   
03F1   F7                     RST   30h   
03F2                          ENDIF      
03F2                          IF   1-ANSI   
                              JR   NZ,ge1   
                              CALL   CONCLS   
                              RST   30h   
                    GE1:      CALL   CONEOL   
                              RST   30h   
03F2                          ENDIF      
03F2                             ; `< and `>. The carry says which: set for the larger. The two are put in
03F2                             ; order, HL the smaller and DE the larger, and then swapped for ">".
03F2                             ; b < a (signed) is the borrow of b - a, turned round if the two signs
03F2                             ; differ: RRA puts the borrow in bit 7, where the two XORs meet it.
03F2   37           G_MAX:    SCF      ; ("<" comes in with the carry clear)
03F3   D1           G_MIN:    POP   DE   ; DE = a, HL = b
03F4   F5                     PUSH   AF   
03F5   7D                     LD   A,L   
03F6   93                     SUB   E   
03F7   7C                     LD   A,H   
03F8   9A                     SBC   A,D   
03F9   1F                     RRA      
03FA   AC                     XOR   H   
03FB   AA                     XOR   D   
03FC   17                     RLA      ; carry: b < a
03FD   38 01                  JR   C,gm2   
03FF   EB                     EX   DE,HL   
0400   F1           GM2:      POP   AF   
0401   30 01                  JR   NC,gm3   
0403   EB                     EX   DE,HL   
0404   F7           GM3:      RST   30h   
0405                          IF   ANSI   
0405                             ; `? ( flag -- ): ESC [ ? 2 5 l hides the cursor, ESC [ ? 2 5 h shows it.
0405   CD 33 04     G_CUR:    CALL   csi   
0408   3E 3F                  LD   A,"?"   
040A   EF                     RST   28h   
040B   3E 32                  LD   A,"2"   
040D   EF                     RST   28h   
040E   3E 35                  LD   A,"5"   
0410   EF                     RST   28h   
0411   7C                     LD   A,H   
0412   B5                     OR   L   
0413   3E 6C                  LD   A,"l"   
0415   28 02                  JR   Z,gc1   
0417   3E 68                  LD   A,"h"   
0419   EF           GC1:      RST   28h   
041A   DF                     RST   18h   
041B                             ; `@ ( row col -- ): ESC [ row+1 ; col+1 H. (ANSI counts from 1.)
041B   D1           G_AT:     POP   DE   ; DE = the row
041C   C5                     PUSH   BC   ; (pdec uses BC)
041D   E5                     PUSH   HL   ; the column
041E   EB                     EX   DE,HL   
041F   CD 33 04               CALL   csi   
0422   23                     INC   HL   
0423   CD 6F 03               CALL   pdec   
0426   3E 3B                  LD   A,";"   
0428   EF                     RST   28h   
0429   E1                     POP   HL   
042A   23                     INC   HL   
042B   CD 6F 03               CALL   pdec   
042E   3E 48                  LD   A,"H"   
0430   EF                     RST   28h   
0431   C1                     POP   BC   
0432   DF                     RST   18h   
0433                             ; csi: print ESC [, which starts every ANSI sequence. Keeps all but A.
0433   3E 1B        CSI:      LD   A,27   
0435   EF                     RST   28h   
0436   3E 5B                  LD   A,"["   
0438   EF                     RST   28h   
0439   C9                     RET      
043A                          ENDIF      
043A                          IF   1-ANSI   
                                 ; With ANSI = 0 the machine's own routines do the work (see the equates).
                    G_CUR:    LD   A,H   
                              OR   L   
                              CALL   CONCUR   
                              RST   18h   
                    G_AT:     POP   DE   ; DE = the row, HL = the column
                              CALL   CONAT   
                              RST   18h   
043A                          ENDIF      
043A                             ; =============================================================================
043A                             ;  Dispatch table: the low byte of each handler's address, in code order
043A                             ;  (the table itself is the macro PTABLE, defined above the dispatcher).
043A                             ;  It must not cross a page (the dispatcher only adds to its low byte).
043A                             ; =============================================================================
043A                             ; The handlers of the first NPG1 characters start in the image's second page.
043A                             ; ] \ [ @ sit where the two pages meet, and which side each lands on
043A                             ; differs between the builds, so the count is worked out here.
043A                             ; (One division to a line: asm80 only rounds down when it stores a value.)
043A                PGRET:    EQU   (h_ret-BASE)/256   ; 0 = first page, 1 = second
043A                PGBRK:    EQU   (h_break-BASE)/256   
043A                PGDEF:    EQU   (h_def-BASE)/256   
043A                PGFET:    EQU   (h_fetch-BASE)/256   
043A                NPG1:     EQU   21 + PGFET + PGDEF + PGBRK + PGRET   
043A                          IF   1-TABP0   
043A                PTAB:        
043A                          ;*Macro unroll:  PTABLE
043A   93                     DB   h_store & 0FFh   
043B   98                     DB   h_str & 0FFh   
043C   B3                     DB   h_num & 0FFh   
043D   9F                     DB   h_print & 0FFh   
043E   8E                     DB   h_swap & 0FFh   
043F   36                     DB   h_and & 0FFh   
0440   B0                     DB   h_emit & 0FFh   
0441   12                     DB   h_open & 0FFh   
0442   1A                     DB   h_close & 0FFh   
0443   57                     DB   h_mul & 0FFh   
0444   2D                     DB   h_add & 0FFh   
0445   DA                     DB   h_cfetch & 0FFh   
0446   25                     DB   h_sub & 0FFh   
0447   90                     DB   h_cstore & 0FFh   
0448   6B                     DB   h_div & 0FFh   
0449   8C                     DB   h_dup & 0FFh   
044A   92                     DB   h_drop & 0FFh   
044B   3E                     DB   h_lt & 0FFh   
044C   4D                     DB   h_eq & 0FFh   
044D   3F                     DB   h_gt & 0FFh   
044E   B9                     DB   h_key & 0FFh   
044F   0D                     DB   h_fetch & 0FFh   
0450   F0                     DB   h_def & 0FFh   
0451   E3                     DB   h_break & 0FFh   
0452   DF                     DB   h_ret & 0FFh   
0453   7F                     DB   h_xor & 0FFh   
0454   92                     DB   h_alloc & 0FFh   
0455   CD                     DB   h_grave & 0FFh   
0456   2C                     DB   h_tor & 0FFh   
0457   87                     DB   h_or & 0FFh   
0458   1C                     DB   h_fromr & 0FFh   
0459   8F                     DB   h_not & 0FFh   
045A                PTABEND:      
045A                          ENDIF      
045A                             ; hexc: if the character at IP is a hex digit (0-9, A-F, a-f), step over it
045A                             ; and return its value in A with the carry set; otherwise leave the IP and
045A                             ; return with the carry clear.
045A   0A           HEXC:     LD   A,(BC)   
045B   D6 30                  SUB   "0"   
045D   FE 0A                  CP   10   
045F   38 09                  JR   C,hc1   
0461   E6 DF                  AND   0DFh   
0463   D6 11                  SUB   11h   
0465   FE 06                  CP   6   
0467   D0                     RET   NC   
0468   D6 F6                  SUB   0F6h   ; + 10, and sets the carry
046A   03           HC1:      INC   BC   
046B   C9                     RET      
046C                             ; =============================================================================
046C                             ;  Console layer. rawk is the host's key routine: a waiting key in A (zero
046C                             ;  flag clear), or A = 0 with the zero flag set when none is waiting. putc
046C                             ;  (RST 28h) prints A. Both keep BC, DE, HL and HL'. In the generic build
046C                             ;  they are the host's KEY and CONOUT routines themselves.
046C                             ; 
046C                             ;  A running program reads the keyboard only through getk and pollk, which
046C                             ;  between them give the break key its rules:
046C                             ;    - Ctrl-C stops the program;
046C                             ;    - any other key that the break check reads is held in KEYBUF for the
046C                             ;      next "?", and a newer one takes its place;
046C                             ;    - "?" (getk) takes the held key first;
046C                             ;    - a program that has stored a non-zero byte at BRKOFF gets Ctrl-C as a
046C                             ;      key like any other, but two of them within about 250 ms still stop it.
046C                             ;  Both are called straight from a handler, never from a routine under one:
046C                             ;  the checked build's report counts on finding one return address above the
046C                             ;  data stack.
046C                             ; =============================================================================
046C                          IFN   CPM   
                    RAWK:     EQU   KEY   
046C                          ENDIF      
046C                             ; pollk: the break check (see rpushn).
046C   CD AA 04     POLLK:    CALL   rawk   
046F   C8                     RET   Z   ; no key
0470   32 7A 07               LD   (KEYBUF),A   ; held for the next "?"
0473   FE 03        PK1:      CP   3   ; (getk joins here)
0475   C0                     RET   NZ   
0476                             ; ctlc: Ctrl-C has been read. If the break key is on, that is the end. If
0476                             ; the program has turned it off, wait about 250 ms for one more key: a
0476                             ; second Ctrl-C is the end too; any other key is held (the newest wins),
0476                             ; and the Ctrl-C goes to the program: returns A = 3, zero flag clear.
0476   3A 7B 07     CTLC:     LD   A,(BRKOFF)   
0479   B7                     OR   A   
047A   CA 15 01     CT0:      JP   Z,brk   
047D   D5                     PUSH   DE   
047E   11 10 27               LD   DE,250*MSLOOP   
0481   CD AA 04     CT1:      CALL   rawk   
0484   20 05                  JR   NZ,ct2   
0486   1B                     DEC   DE   
0487   7A                     LD   A,D   
0488   B3                     OR   E   
0489   20 F6                  JR   NZ,ct1   
048B   D1           CT2:      POP   DE   ; A = the second key, or 0 if none came
048C   FE 03                  CP   3   
048E   28 EA                  JR   Z,ct0   ; (the zero flag takes the JP there)
0490   B7                     OR   A   
0491   28 03                  JR   Z,ct3   
0493   32 7A 07               LD   (KEYBUF),A   
0496   3E 03        CT3:      LD   A,3   
0498   B7                     OR   A   
0499   C9                     RET      
049A                             ; getk: a key for "?", or A = 0 and the zero flag if there is none.
049A   E5           GETK:     PUSH   HL   ; a held key goes first, and is taken out of
049B   21 7A 07               LD   HL,KEYBUF   ;   the buffer
049E   7E                     LD   A,(HL)   
049F   36 00                  LD   (HL),0   
04A1   E1                     POP   HL   
04A2   B7                     OR   A   
04A3   C0                     RET   NZ   
04A4   CD AA 04               CALL   rawk   
04A7   C8                     RET   Z   
04A8   18 C9                  JR   pk1   ; Ctrl-C? If not, that is the key
04AA                          IF   (1-CHECKED)*(1-EDITOR)   
04AA                BRK:      EQU   endprog   ; the unchecked build stops without a word
04AA                          ENDIF      ;   (with the editor, both stacks are cleared);
04AA                          IF   (1-CHECKED)*EDITOR   
                    BRK:      EQU   edit0   
04AA                          ENDIF      
04AA                          IF   CHECKED   
                    BRK:      EQU   e_break   ;   the checked build reports B
04AA                          ENDIF      
04AA                          IF   CPM   
04AA   3E FF        RAWK:     LD   A,0FFh   ; BDOS 6 with E = FFh: a key, or 0
04AC                             ; putc: BDOS 6 for every character. BDOS 2 would check for ^S while
04AC                             ; printing and could swallow a key that BDOS 6 then never sees.
04AC   D5           PUTC:     PUSH   DE   
04AD   E5                     PUSH   HL   
04AE   5F                     LD   E,A   
04AF   3E 06                  LD   A,6   
04B1   CD B8 04               CALL   bdosx   
04B4   E1                     POP   HL   
04B5   D1                     POP   DE   
04B6   B7                     OR   A   ; (for getk)
04B7   C9                     RET      
04B8                             ; bdosx: call BDOS function A with DE, keeping BC and HL'
04B8   C5           BDOSX:    PUSH   BC   
04B9   D9                     EXX      
04BA   E5                     PUSH   HL   
04BB   D9                     EXX      
04BC   4F                     LD   C,A   
04BD   CD 05 00               CALL   BDOS   
04C0   D9                     EXX      
04C1   E1                     POP   HL   
04C2   D9                     EXX      
04C3   C1                     POP   BC   
04C4   C9                     RET      
04C5                          ENDIF      
04C5                             ; =============================================================================
04C5                             ;  Checked build: the checks and the error report
04C5                             ; =============================================================================
04C5                          IF   CHECKED   
                                 ; chkstk: both stacks are checked once per character, not in every handler.
                                 ; The data stack is right when SP lies in the 256 bytes below DSTOP: adding
                                 ; the constant carries if it is above (cells were popped that were never
                                 ; pushed), and leaves a high byte of FFh if it is in range. Errors are found
                                 ; a character late at most: the bytes above DSTOP and the guard band below
                                 ; the page take what happens meanwhile. DE is free between characters.
                    CHKSTK:   EX   DE,HL   
                              LD   HL,(1-DSTOP)&0FFFFh   ; (SP is 2 lower here: the call)
                              ADD   HL,SP   
                              EX   DE,HL   
                              JR   C,e_under   
                              INC   D   
                              JR   NZ,e_over   
                              EXX      ; the return stack: in its page (or it has
                              LD   A,H   ;   overflowed), and not above its empty
                              CP   RSPAGE   ;   position (an underflow stays inside the
                              LD   A,L   ;   page, in the guard band)
                              EXX      
                              JR   NZ,e_rover   
                              CP   RSTOP&0FFh+1   
                              RET   C   
                              EXX      ; return stack underflow: it counts as empty
                              LD   L,RSTOP&0FFh   ;   (H is right: the pointer is in its page)
                              EXX      
                              LD   A,"r"   
                              JR   errp   
                    E_ROVER:   LD   A,"R"   ; return stack overflow
                              DB   11h   ; (LD DE,nn hides the next entry)
                    E_OVER:   LD   A,"S"   ; data stack overflow
                              JR   errp   
                    E_UNDER:   LD   SP,DSTOP   ; data stack underflow: it counts as empty
                              LD   A,"s"   
                              JR   error   
                                 ; e_hi: the inner loop read a reserved byte, 80h-FFh: X. But a word cell that
                                 ; was never defined still holds 0000h, and the byte there is a reserved one
                                 ; in every build (AFh or C3h): if the IP is in page zero, this was a call of
                                 ; an undefined word. The call is undone, so the place is the call itself.
                    E_HI:     INC   B   
                              DJNZ   e_resv   ; (B is as it was, and is not 0)
                              RST   08h   
                              LD   B,D   
                              LD   C,E   
                              LD   A,"U"   
                              JR   error   
                                 ; chkhp: HL = the new heap top, DE = the old one, the carry is from adding
                                 ; the count. Stop if the top is not below the limit page, or is below the
                                 ; program's end.
                    CHKHP:       
04C5                          ENDIF      
04C5                          IF   CHECKED*CPM   
                                 ; With this much room a top that wrapped round can land back in
                                 ; range, so the add is tested too: growing (A, the count's high
                                 ; byte, is positive) must not carry, and releasing must.
                              RRA      ; the carry comes in above the sign:
                              ADD   A,40h   ;   bit 7 = carry XOR sign
                              ADD   A,A   
                              JR   C,e_heap   
                              LD   A,(0007h)   
                              DEC   A   
                              CP   H   
                              JR   C,e_heap   
04C5                          ENDIF      
04C5                          IF   CHECKED*(1-CPM)   
                                 ; (Here the program's space is under 32K, so a top that wrapped
                                 ; round always falls outside it.)
                              LD   A,H   
                              CP   HEAPLIM   
                              JR   NC,e_heap   
04C5                          ENDIF      
04C5                          IF   CHECKED   
                              PUSH   DE   
                              EX   DE,HL   
                              LD   HL,(NPEND)   
                              ADD   HL,DE   ; carry: at or above the program's end
                              EX   DE,HL   
                              POP   DE   
                              RET   C   
                    E_HEAP:   OR   A   ; put the count back in TOS for the report
                              SBC   HL,DE   
                              LD   A,"H"   
                              JR   errp   
                                 ; chkst: stop unless HL is in the program's own space: from the letter page
                                 ; up to the heap limit (the OS, or HEAPLIM), so the interpreter's stacks and
                                 ; whatever lies above the limit are safe. Memory above the heap top but
                                 ; below the limit is the program's own: Tiny BASIC keeps its lines there.
                                 ; It is the page of HL + 1 that is tested, so that one test serves both
                                 ; bytes of a cell: the last byte below the limit can"t be stored to with ".'.
                                 ; Keeps HL and BC. It runs on into its own error entry.
                    CHKST:    INC   HL   
                              LD   A,H   
                              DEC   HL   
                              CP   LETPAGE   
                              JR   C,e_store   
04C5                          ENDIF      
04C5                          IF   CHECKED*(1-CPM)   
                              CP   HEAPLIM   
                              RET   C   
04C5                          ENDIF      
04C5                          IF   CHECKED*CPM   
                              LD   E,A   
                              LD   A,(0007h)   ; the BDOS page is the heap limit
                              DEC   A   
                              CP   E   
                              RET   NC   
04C5                          ENDIF      
04C5                          IF   CHECKED   
                                 ; Error entries. Each loads its letter and then hides the next entry inside
                                 ; a 3-byte LD DE,nn (the 11h), so they all fall through to `error`.
                    E_STORE:   LD   A,"O"   ; a store outside the program's space
                              DB   11h   
                    E_BREAK:   LD   A,"B"   ; Ctrl-C (found inside pollk or getk)
                                 ; errp: an error found inside a routine: drop its return address first.
                    ERRP:     POP   DE   
                              JR   error   
                    E_DOLLAR:   POP   DE   ; "$" ran into a NUL: drop prstr's return
                              POP   HL   ;   address, put the string's address back in
                              DB   11h   ;   TOS, and step over the next two bytes: Q
                    E_QUOTE:   LD   B,H   ; an unclosed string: HL is its address, one
                              LD   C,L   ;   past the opening quote, which is the place
                              LD   A,"Q"   
                              DB   11h   
                    E_RESV:   LD   A,"X"   ; a reserved byte outside a string
                              DB   11h   
                    E_ZERO:   LD   A,"Z"   ; dividing by zero
                              DB   11h   
                    E_BRACK:   LD   A,"W"   ; bad character after [
                                 ; error: the report, then the end. A = the letter, BC = one past the place,
                                 ; HL = TOS, and both stacks as the report is to show them:
                                 ; 
                                 ;   Err X @ line,col
                                 ;   Stk n: the top 8 cells at most, bottom to top
                                 ;   Rtn n
                    ERROR:    PUSH   HL   ; now the whole data stack is in memory
                              LD   E,A   
                              CALL   pnl   
                              DB   "Err ",22h   
                              LD   A,E   
                              RST   28h   
                              CALL   pmsg   
                              DB   " @ ",22h   
                              DEC   BC   ; BC = the place
                                 ; The line and column. A place below the program is in the line
                                 ; buffer: line 0. Otherwise count the LFs from the program's start;
                                 ; DE = the line's number, HL = where it starts.
                              LD   HL,LINEBUF   
                              LD   DE,0   
                              LD   A,B   
                              CP   PROG/256   
                              JR   C,er3   
                              INC   H   
                              LD   L,E   ; HL = PROG
                    ER1:      INC   DE   ; a new line starts at HL
                              PUSH   HL   
                    ER2:      LD   A,L   
                              SUB   C   
                              LD   A,H   
                              SBC   A,B   
                              JR   NC,er2x   ; reached the place
                              LD   A,(HL)   
                              INC   HL   
                              CP   10   
                              JR   NZ,er2   
                              POP   AF   
                              JR   er1   
                    ER2X:     POP   HL   
                    ER3:      PUSH   BC   
                              PUSH   HL   
                              EX   DE,HL   
                              CALL   pdec   ; the line
                              LD   A,","   
                              RST   28h   
                              POP   DE   
                              POP   HL   
                              OR   A   
                              SBC   HL,DE   
                              INC   HL   
                              CALL   pdec   ; the column
                                 ; The two stack lines:  Stk n: the top 8 cells at most, bottom to top
                                 ;                       Rtn n
                                 ; TOS is in memory with the rest (pushed).
                              CALL   pnl   
                              DB   "Stk ",22h   
                              LD   HL,(2-DSTOP)&0FFFFh   ; SP - (DSTOP-2) is minus twice the
                              ADD   HL,SP   ;   depth (the cell at DSTOP-2 was pushed
                              RST   20h   ;   with the first value and holds nothing)
                              CALL   phalf   ; the depth
                              LD   A,":"   
                              RST   28h   
                              LD   A,C   
                              CP   9   
                              JR   C,er6   
                              CALL   pmsg   
                              DB   " ...",22h   
                              LD   C,8   
                    ER6:      LD   H,B   ; C = the number of cells to show (B is 0:
                                 ;   phalf left the depth in BC)
                              LD   L,C   
                              ADD   HL,HL   
                              ADD   HL,SP   ; HL -> just above the deepest of them
                              INC   C   
                    ER7:      DEC   C   
                              JR   Z,er8   
                              DEC   HL   
                              LD   D,(HL)   
                              DEC   HL   
                              LD   E,(HL)   
                              PUSH   HL   
                              PUSH   BC   
                              LD   A," "   
                              RST   28h   
                              EX   DE,HL   
                              CALL   psgn   
                              POP   BC   
                              POP   HL   
                              JR   er7   
                    ER8:      CALL   pnl   
                              DB   "Rtn ",22h   
                              EXX      ; twice the depth is RSTOP less the pointer:
                              LD   A,RSTOP&0FFh   ;   the low bytes are enough, since even an
                              SUB   L   ;   overflowing stack holds under 128 entries
                              EXX      
                              LD   L,A   
                              LD   H,B   ; (B is still 0)
                              CALL   phalf   
                              CALL   pnl   
                              DB   22h   
04C5                          ENDIF      
04C5                          IF   CHECKED*(1-EDITOR)   
                              JP   endprog   
04C5                          ENDIF      
04C5                          IF   CHECKED*EDITOR   
                              JP   edit0   ; back to the editor, with both stacks cleared
04C5                          ENDIF      
04C5                          IF   CHECKED   
                                 ; phalf: print half of HL, and leave it in C.
                    PHALF:    SRL   H   
                              RR   L   
                              PUSH   HL   
                              CALL   pdec   
                              POP   BC   
                              RET      
                                 ; prstr: print the string at HL, to its closing quote, decoding "/" (this is
                                 ; "$", and the texts of the report). A
                                 ; NUL first is an error: Q.
                    PRSTR:    LD   A,(HL)   
                              INC   HL   
                              CP   22h   
                              RET   Z   
                              OR   A   
                              JP   Z,e_dollar   
                              CP   "/"   
                              JR   NZ,prs1   
                              LD   A,(HL)   
                              INC   HL   
                              AND   0BFh   
                    PRS1:     RST   28h   
                              JR   prstr   
                                 ; pmsg: print the text that follows the CALL, to its closing quote. Keeps HL.
                                 ; pnl: the same, on a new line.
                    PNL:      LD   A,13   
                              RST   28h   
                              LD   A,10   
                              RST   28h   
                    PMSG:     EX   (SP),HL   
                              CALL   prstr   
                              EX   (SP),HL   
                              RET      
04C5                          ENDIF      
04C5                             ; =============================================================================
04C5                             ;  The line editor (EDITOR = 1)
04C5                             ; 
04C5                             ;  The interpreter starts here, and a program that ends comes back here.
04C5                             ;  There is no prompt. It follows the spec's suggested standard for a line
04C5                             ;  editor (docs/b8script.md, Environments). Type a line and press Return:
04C5                             ; 
04C5                             ;    n text    put the text in as line n; the lines from n on move down. A
04C5                             ;              number past the end (or 0) adds the line at the end.
04C5                             ;    n         take line n out
04C5                             ;    anything else is run at once, as B8Script. (Start such a line with a
04C5                             ;    space if it would begin with a digit.)
04C5                             ; 
04C5                             ;  A command key ends the line too, and takes what was typed as its argument:
04C5                             ; 
04C5                             ;    ^G        run the program
04C5                             ;    n ^L      list from line n (no number: all of it). Any key holds the
04C5                             ;              list until another key is pressed; Ctrl-C ends it.
04C5                             ;    n ^E      put line n in the input line; Return puts it back, changed
04C5                             ;    name ^R   read. CP/M: the file of that name (no name: the same file as
04C5                             ;              last time). Generic: what is typed, or pasted, from now until
04C5                             ;              ^Z replaces the program; it is not echoed.
04C5                             ;    name ^W   write. CP/M: to that file (no name: the same file as last
04C5                             ;              time). Generic: the text is printed, as it is.
04C5                             ;    ^N ^N     new: no program (the key twice in a row)
04C5                             ;    ^X        leave (to LEAVE)
04C5                             ; 
04C5                             ;  In the line: ^B and ^F, or the left and right arrow keys, move the cursor;
04C5                             ;  a character goes in at the cursor; Backspace and DEL take out the one
04C5                             ;  before it; Esc drops the line. Only CR, LF, BS and printing characters are
04C5                             ;  sent to the terminal, so any terminal will do.
04C5                             ; 
04C5                             ;  Lines are counted, not numbered: the text holds no line numbers, and the
04C5                             ;  list shows each line's place. There can be 65535 lines. A typed line holds
04C5                             ;  125 characters; the one character after a line number separates it from
04C5                             ;  the text and is not stored. The text is kept as it is typed, each line
04C5                             ;  ending in CR LF, at PROG.
04C5                             ; 
04C5                             ;  What lasts from one line to the next: the program, the words, the
04C5                             ;  variables and the data stack. An error or a break clears both stacks. The
04C5                             ;  return stack starts empty for every line.
04C5                             ; 
04C5                             ;  Things to know:
04C5                             ;    - Reset empties the program (generic builds).
04C5                             ;    - A word's address points into the program, so run the program again
04C5                             ;      after editing it.
04C5                             ;    - Nothing is printed between a program's output and what is typed next.
04C5                             ;    - A line run at once sits in the line buffer, which -n? also reads into:
04C5                             ;      a line that calls -n? and carries on afterwards runs what was typed.
04C5                             ;      (The stored program never comes back to the line, so it may.)
04C5                             ;    - The editor"s own keys are not the program"s: -n? is the plain line
04C5                             ;      read of the other builds (BDOS 10 under CP/M).
04C5                             ; 
04C5                             ;  The data stack is the CPU's stack, so the editor works on top of whatever
04C5                             ;  the last line left there, with TOS pushed like the rest.
04C5                             ; =============================================================================
04C5                          IF   EDGEN   
                    INIT:        ; reset (A = 0)
04C5                          ENDIF      
04C5                          IF   EDGEN*CHECKED   
                                 ; Clear the lower half of the letter page: every variable starts at 0, and
                                 ; every word cell holds 0000h, the address an undefined word is caught at
                                 ; (see e_hi).
                              LD   HL,LET   
                    INI1:     LD   (HL),A   
                              INC   L   
                              JP   P,ini1   ; +00h to +7Fh
04C5                          ENDIF      
04C5                          IF   EDGEN   
                              JR   edit0   
04C5                          ENDIF      
04C5                          IF   EDITOR   
                                 ; ^F, right arrow: one to the right, by printing the character there
                    RIGHT:    LD   A,L   
                              CP   E   
                              JR   Z,ed1   ; at the end
                              LD   A,(HL)   
                              INC   L   
                              JR   lf1   
                                 ; Esc: alone it drops the line. An arrow key sends Esc [ and a letter, so
                                 ; wait about 5 ms for a second key: after a "[" read on to the letter that
                                 ; ends the sequence, and act on C (right) and D (left).
                    ESC:      LD   BC,5*MSLOOP   
                    ES1:      CALL   rawk   
                              JR   NZ,es2   
                              DEC   BC   
                              LD   A,B   
                              OR   C   
                              JR   NZ,es1   
                              CALL   fin   ; no second key: the line is dropped
                              JR   edit   
                    ES2:      CP   "["   
                              JR   NZ,ed1   ; not a sequence known here
                    ES3:      CALL   ekey   
                              CP   40h   
                              JR   C,es3   ; (its parameters)
                              SUB   "C"   
                              JR   Z,right   
                              DEC   A   ; "D"?
                              JR   NZ,ed1   ; no: on into left
                                 ; ^B, left arrow: the cursor goes one to the left
                    LEFT:     LD   A,L   
                              ADD   A,A   
                              JR   Z,ed1   ; (L = 80h: at the start)
                              DEC   L   
                              LD   A,8   
                    LF1:      RST   28h   
                              JR   ed1   
                                 ; edit0: reset, an error or a break: both stacks are cleared.
                                 ; skend: a program that ended inside skip: its return address goes.
                                 ; edend: a program that ended: TOS joins the rest of the data stack.
                    EDIT0:    LD   SP,DSTOP-2   ; empty (the cell that stands for TOS is pushed)
                              DB   21h   ; (LD HL,nn: steps over the next two bytes)
                    SKEND:    POP   DE   
                    EDEND:    PUSH   HL   
                                 ; edit: start a new input line.
                    EDIT:     EXX      
                              LD   HL,RSTOP   ; the return stack is empty
                              EXX      
                              LD   HL,0   
                              LD   (KEYBUF),HL   ; no key is held, and the break key is on
                              LD   (EDLN),HL   ; no line is being edited
                              LD   HL,LINEBUF   ; HL = the cursor,
                              LD   E,L   ;   E = the end of the line (its low byte)
                    ED1:      CALL   ekey   
                              CP   7Fh   
                              JR   Z,bsp   ; DEL
                              CP   " "   
                              JR   NC,insc   
                              CP   9   
                              JR   Z,insc   ; Tab is text
                              CP   8   
                              JR   Z,bsp   
                              CP   2   
                              JR   Z,left   ; ^B
                              CP   6   
                              JR   Z,right   ; ^F
                              CP   1Bh   
                              JR   Z,esc   
                              PUSH   HL   ; a command key? Look it up
                              LD   HL,cmds   
                              LD   B,NCMD   
                    ED2:      CP   (HL)   
                              INC   HL   
                              JR   Z,ed3   
                              INC   HL   
                              INC   HL   
                              DJNZ   ed2   
                              POP   HL   
                              JR   ed1   ; no: the key is ignored
                    ED3:      LD   A,(HL)   
                              INC   HL   
                              LD   H,(HL)   
                              LD   L,A   
                              EX   (SP),HL   ; the command's address: fin returns to it
                                 ; fin: end the input line: CR LF and a NUL after it, and a new line on the
                                 ; terminal. Leaves BC -> the line and HL -> the NUL.
                    FIN:      LD   H,LETPAGE   
                              LD   L,E   
                              LD   (HL),13   
                              INC   L   
                              LD   (HL),10   
                              DEC   L   
                              CALL   prl   ; (prints the CR LF)
                              LD   (HL),0   
                              LD   BC,LINEBUF   
                              RET      
                                 ; Backspace, DEL: the character before the cursor goes. The cursor moves
                                 ; left, the rest of the line moves down over it, and the last place (now a
                                 ; space) is printed over along with the rest.
                    BSP:      LD   A,L   
                              ADD   A,A   
                              JR   Z,ed1   ; at the start
                              DEC   L   
                              LD   A,8   
                              RST   28h   
                              PUSH   HL   
                    BS1:      INC   L   
                              LD   A,(HL)   
                              DEC   L   
                              LD   (HL),A   
                              INC   L   
                              LD   A,L   
                              CP   E   
                              JR   NZ,bs1   
                              DEC   L   
                              LD   (HL)," "   
                              POP   HL   
                              LD   D,E   
                              DEC   E   
                              JR   ic2   
                                 ; A character goes in at the cursor: it ripples up through the rest of the
                                 ; line, the cursor moves on, and the rest is printed again.
                    INSC:     LD   B,A   
                              LD   A,E   
                              CP   0FDh   
                              JR   Z,ed1   ; the line is full: 125 characters
                              LD   A,B   
                              RST   28h   
                              PUSH   HL   
                    IC1:      LD   A,(HL)   
                              LD   (HL),B   
                              LD   B,A   
                              LD   A,L   
                              INC   L   
                              CP   E   
                              JR   NZ,ic1   
                              POP   HL   
                              INC   L   
                              INC   E   
                              LD   D,E   
                    IC2:      CALL   tail   
                              JR   ed1   
                                 ; tail: print the line from the cursor to D (a low byte), and bring the
                                 ; cursor back with backspaces. Nothing at all if the cursor is at D.
                    TAIL:     LD   C,L   
                    TA1:      LD   A,L   
                              CP   D   
                              JR   Z,ta2   
                              LD   A,(HL)   
                              RST   28h   
                              INC   L   
                              JR   ta1   
                    TA2:      LD   A,L   
                              CP   C   
                              RET   Z   
                              LD   A,8   
                              RST   28h   
                              DEC   L   
                              JR   ta2   
                                 ; ekey: wait for a key
                    EKEY:     CALL   rawk   
                              JR   Z,ekey   
                              RET      
                                 ; The command keys, and where each goes (after fin).
                    CMDS:     DB   13   
                              DW   cret   
                              DB   7   ; ^G
                              DW   crun   
                              DB   12   ; ^L
                              DW   clist   
                              DB   5   ; ^E
                              DW   cedln   
                              DB   18   ; ^R
                              DW   cread   
                              DB   23   ; ^W
                              DW   cwrite   
                              DB   14   ; ^N
                              DW   cnew   
                              DB   24   ; ^X
                              DW   LEAVE   
                    NCMD:     EQU   8   
                                 ; ^N ^N: no program, if the next key is ^N too
                    CNEW:     CALL   ekey   
                              CP   14   
                              JR   NZ,ged0   
                              XOR   A   
                              LD   (PROG),A   
                    GED0:     JR   gedit   
                                 ; ^E: line n goes into the input line, to be changed. EDLN remembers which
                                 ; line it was: Return puts the text back in its place.
                    CEDLN:    CALL   rdnum   
                              LD   (EDLN),HL   ; (no such line: `edit` clears it again)
                              CALL   find   ; HL -> the line, or the NUL if there is none
                              LD   A,(HL)   
                              OR   A   
                              JR   Z,ged0   
                              LD   DE,LINEBUF   
                    CE1:      LD   A,(HL)   ; copy it, and show it, up to its CR (or LF)
                              CP   13   
                              JR   Z,ce2   
                              CP   10   
                              JR   Z,ce2   
                              LD   (DE),A   
                              RST   28h   
                              INC   HL   
                              INC   E   
                              LD   A,E   
                              CP   0FDh   ; (a longer line is cut at 125 characters)
                              JR   NZ,ce1   
                    CE2:      EX   DE,HL   ; the cursor is at the line's end
                              LD   E,L   
                              JP   ed1   
                                 ; Return. If ^E put a line here, the text goes back in its place. If not:
                                 ; a number and text is a line to put in, a number alone a line to take out,
                                 ; and anything else is run where it is.
                    CRET:     PUSH   HL   ; the end of what was typed
                              LD   HL,(EDLN)   
                              LD   A,H   
                              OR   L   
                              JR   Z,cr1   
                              PUSH   HL   
                              CALL   delln   
                              POP   HL   
                              JR   ins   
                    CR1:      CALL   rdnum   ; HL = the number it starts with, BC -> after
                              LD   A,C   ; C is still 80h if there was no number:
                              ADD   A,A   ;   only then is twice it 0
                              JR   Z,st0p   ; no number: run the line
                              LD   A,(BC)   
                              CP   13   
                              JR   NZ,cr2   
                              POP   DE   ; the number alone: take that line out
                              CALL   delln   
                              JR   gedit   
                    CR2:      INC   BC   ; step over the one character after the number
                                 ; Put the text at BC in as line n (in HL): open a gap of its length there,
                                 ; CR and LF included, and copy it in.
                    INS:      CALL   find   ; HL -> where it goes
                              POP   DE   ; the end of what was typed
                              LD   A,E   
                              SUB   C   ; A = the length of the text, with its CR LF
                              PUSH   BC   ; the text
                              LD   C,A   
                              LD   B,0   
                              PUSH   BC   ; its length
                              LD   D,H   
                              LD   E,L   ; DE = where it goes
                              XOR   A   
                              LD   C,A   ; BC = 0: CPIR looks as far as it needs to
                              CPIR      ; HL -> one past the program's NUL
                              SBC   HL,DE   ; the number of bytes to move up, NUL included
                              LD   B,H   
                              LD   C,L   
                              ADD   HL,DE   
                              DEC   HL   ; HL -> the NUL
                              EX   DE,HL   
                              EX   (SP),HL   ; HL = the length; where it goes is kept
                              PUSH   HL   
                              ADD   HL,DE   ; the NUL's new place
                              EX   DE,HL   
                              LDDR      ; move the rest of the program up
                              POP   BC   ; the length
                              POP   DE   ; where it goes
                              POP   HL   ; the text
                              LDIR      
                    GEDIT:    JP   edit   
                                 ; ^G: run the program. st0p: run the typed line (BC -> it).
                    CRUN:     LD   BC,PROG   
                              DB   3Eh   ; (LD A,n: steps over the POP)
                    ST0P:     POP   HL   ; (the end of what was typed)
                                 ; st0: start running at BC. The heap starts after the stored program's NUL.
                    ST0:      LD   HL,PROG   
                              XOR   A   
                    ST1:      CP   (HL)   
                              INC   HL   
                              JR   NZ,st1   
                              LD   (HEAP),HL   
04C5                          ENDIF      
04C5                          IF   EDITOR*CHECKED   
                              RST   20h   ; minus the heap"s first address: "_' may not
                              LD   (NPEND),HL   ;   release below it
04C5                          ENDIF      
04C5                          IF   EDITOR   
                              POP   HL   ; TOS: the data stack is as the last line left it
                              RST   30h   ; (its return address is thrown away)
                                 ; ^L: list from line n. DE = the number of the line at HL.
                    CLIST:    CALL   rdnum   ; HL = n, or 0 if there was none:
                              LD   A,H   
                              OR   L   
                              JR   NZ,li0   
                              INC   L   ;   then from line 1
                    LI0:      PUSH   HL   
                              CALL   find   
                              POP   DE   
                    LI1:      LD   A,(HL)   
                              OR   A   
                              JR   Z,gedit   ; the end of the text
                              CALL   rawk   
                              JR   Z,li3   ; no key: carry on
                              CP   3   
                              CALL   NZ,ekey   ; any key but Ctrl-C: wait for one more
                              CP   3   
                              JR   Z,gedit   ; Ctrl-C, first or second, ends the list
                    LI3:      PUSH   HL   
                              PUSH   DE   
                              EX   DE,HL   
                              CALL   pdec   ; the line's number,
                              LD   A," "   
                              RST   28h   ;   a space,
                              POP   DE   
                              POP   HL   
                              INC   DE   
                              CALL   prl   ;   and the line
                              JR   li1   
                                 ; delln: take line n (in HL) out: copy everything after it down over it.
                    DELLN:    CALL   find   
                              LD   D,H   
                              LD   E,L   
                              CALL   nxl   ; HL -> the next line
                    DE1:      LD   A,(HL)   
                              LD   (DE),A   
                              INC   HL   
                              INC   DE   
                              OR   A   
                              JR   NZ,de1   
                              RET      
                                 ; find: HL = a line number. Returns HL -> that line, or -> the NUL at the end
                                 ; of the text if there are fewer lines (or the number is 0). Keeps BC.
                    FIND:     EX   DE,HL   
                              LD   HL,PROG   
                    FI1:      DEC   DE   
                              LD   A,D   
                              OR   E   
                              RET   Z   
                              CALL   nxl   
                              JR   NZ,fi1   
                              RET      
                                 ; nxl: step HL over one line, to just past its LF (and return not-zero), or
                                 ; stop at the NUL that ends the text (and return zero).
                    NXL:      LD   A,(HL)   
                              OR   A   
                              RET   Z   
                              INC   HL   
                              CP   10   
                              JR   NZ,nxl   
                              OR   A   
                              RET      
                                 ; prl: print the line at HL, to its LF; HL -> just past it.
                    PRL:      LD   A,(HL)   
                              RST   28h   
                              LD   A,(HL)   
                              INC   HL   
                              CP   10   
                              JR   NZ,prl   
                              RET      
04C5                          ENDIF      
04C5                          IF   EDGEN   
                                 ; ^R, generic: what comes in from now until ^Z is the program. A CR is
                                 ; stored as CR LF; a LF right after a line end is dropped (it is the CR's
                                 ; own, or an empty line's), and a LF anywhere else ends a line too. A last
                                 ; line with no end is given one. Nothing is echoed, and there is no check
                                 ; for running out of memory.
                    CREAD:    LD   HL,PROG-1   
                              LD   (HL),10   ; (as if a line had just ended: the byte is
                              INC   HL   ;   the line buffer's last, and spare)
                    RD1:      CALL   ekey   
                              LD   C,A   
                              CP   1Ah   
                              JR   NZ,rd2   
                              LD   A,10   ; ^Z ends the last line, as a LF would
                    RD2:      CP   10   
                              JR   NZ,rd3   
                              DEC   HL   
                              CP   (HL)   
                              INC   HL   
                              JR   Z,rd4   ; straight after a line end: dropped
                              LD   A,13   ; anywhere else it ends the line
                    RD3:      LD   (HL),A   
                              INC   HL   
                              CP   13   
                              JR   NZ,rd4   
                              LD   (HL),10   ; after a CR goes a LF
                              INC   HL   
                    RD4:      LD   A,C   
                              CP   1Ah   
                              JR   NZ,rd1   
                              LD   (HL),0   
                    GED1:     JP   edit   
                                 ; ^W, generic: the text is printed as it is, for the terminal to capture.
                    CWRITE:   LD   HL,PROG   
                    CW1:      LD   A,(HL)   
                              OR   A   
                              JR   Z,ged1   
                              RST   28h   
                              INC   HL   
                              JR   cw1   
04C5                          ENDIF      
04C5                          IF   EDITOR*CPM   
                    CFCB:     EQU   005Ch   ; the file's name is kept here, where the CCP
                                 ;   put the one from the command line
                                 ; ^W, CP/M: write the file: delete the old one, make it anew, write the
                                 ; text in records of 128 bytes, and close it. The text's NUL and the 127
                                 ; bytes after it are set to ^Z meanwhile, which pads the last record. (A
                                 ; full disk or directory is not noticed: the calls fail and that is all.)
                    CWRITE:   CALL   setname   
                              LD   C,19   ; delete
                              CALL   fbdos   
                              LD   C,22   ; make
                              CALL   fbdos   
                              LD   HL,PROG   
                              XOR   A   
                    CW1:      CP   (HL)   
                              INC   HL   
                              JR   NZ,cw1   
                              DEC   HL   ; HL -> the NUL
                              PUSH   HL   
                              LD   B,128   
                    CW2:      LD   (HL),1Ah   
                              INC   HL   
                              DJNZ   cw2   
                              POP   HL   
                              LD   DE,PROG   
                    CW3:      LD   A,E   ; a record that starts before the end is written
                              SUB   L   
                              LD   A,D   
                              SBC   A,H   
                              JR   NC,cw4   
                              PUSH   HL   
                              LD   C,21   ; write, from where the record lies
                              CALL   frec   
                              POP   HL   
                              JR   cw3   
                    CW4:      LD   (HL),0   ; the NUL again
                              LD   C,16   ; close,
                              LD   HL,edit   ;   and from there back to the editor
                              PUSH   HL   
                                 ; fbdos: BDOS function C on the file. (^W ends by running on into it.)
                    FBDOS:    LD   DE,CFCB   
                              JP   BDOS   
                                 ; frec: BDOS function C (read or write a record) with the 128 bytes at DE.
                                 ; Returns A = the BDOS's answer, HL = DE and DE = DE + 128.
                    FREC:     PUSH   DE   
                              PUSH   BC   
                              LD   C,26   ; set the DMA address
                              CALL   BDOS   
                              POP   BC   
                              CALL   fbdos   
                              POP   DE   
                              LD   HL,128   
                              ADD   HL,DE   
                              EX   DE,HL   
                              RET      
                                 ; setname: if a name was typed (the line does not start with its CR), put it
                                 ; in the FCB: up to 8 characters, a dot, up to 3 more, in capitals. The drive
                                 ; is the current one. Then, name or no name, clear the FCB after the name,
                                 ; as it must be before a file is opened or made.
                    SETNAME:   LD   DE,LINEBUF   
                              LD   A,(DE)   
                              CP   13   
                              JR   Z,fcbclr   
                              LD   HL,CFCB   
                              LD   (HL),0   ; the current drive
                              LD   B,11   
                    SN1:      INC   L   
                              LD   (HL)," "   
                              DJNZ   sn1   
                              LD   L,CFCB+1   
                    SN2:      LD   A,(DE)   
                              INC   DE   
                              CP   13   
                              JR   Z,fcbclr   
                              CP   "."   
                              JR   NZ,sn3   
                              LD   L,CFCB+9   ; the type
                              JR   sn2   
                    SN3:      CP   "a"   
                              JR   C,sn4   
                              AND   5Fh   ; a capital
                    SN4:      LD   (HL),A   
                              INC   L   
                              JR   sn2   
                    FCBCLR:   LD   HL,CFCB+12   
                              LD   B,24   
                    FC1:      LD   (HL),0   
                              INC   HL   
                              DJNZ   fc1   
                              RET      
                                 ; ^R, CP/M: read the file. A name typed before the key is the file's name
                                 ; from now on. It runs on into load, which returns to the editor.
                    CREAD:    CALL   setname   
                              LD   HL,edit   
                              PUSH   HL   
                                 ; load: read the file into PROG. No such file: no program. The text ends at
                                 ; the file"s first ^Z (1Ah), which pads a text file"s last record; one more
                                 ; goes after the last record, so the search always stops. And every line
                                 ; must end in LF: a last line without one is given a CR LF. (The FCB is
                                 ; clear after its name: the CCP left it so, or setname did.)
                    LOAD:     LD   C,15   ; open (no such file: the first read fails
                              CALL   fbdos   ;   too)
                              LD   DE,PROG   
                    LD1:      LD   C,20   ; read the next 128 bytes
                              CALL   frec   
                              OR   A   
                              JR   Z,ld1   
                              LD   (HL),1Ah   ; (HL = where the record that failed would be)
                              LD   HL,PROG-1   
                              LD   A,10   ; (a file with no text needs nothing added)
                    TR1:      INC   HL   
                              LD   E,A   ; E = the character before this one
                              LD   A,(HL)   
                              CP   1Ah   
                              JR   NZ,tr1   
                              LD   A,E   
                              CP   10   
                              JR   Z,tr2   
                              LD   (HL),13   
                              INC   HL   
                              LD   (HL),10   
                              INC   HL   
                    TR2:      LD   (HL),0   
                              RET      
04C5                          ENDIF      
04C5                             ; =============================================================================
04C5                          IF   CPM   
04C5                             ; The RAM pages follow the image; the heap may grow to the BDOS.
04C5                START:       
04C5                          ENDIF      
04C5                          IF   CPM*CHECKED   
                                 ; Clear the lower half of the letter page: every variable starts at
                                 ; 0, every word cell holds 0000h, the address an undefined word is
                                 ; caught at (see e_hi: the byte there is CP/M's JP, C3h), and no key
                                 ; is held back.
                              LD   HL,LET   
                              XOR   A   
                    INI1:     LD   (HL),A   
                              INC   L   
                              JP   P,ini1   ; +00h to +7Fh
04C5                          ENDIF      
04C5                          IF   CPM   
04C5   21 08 01               LD   HL,vecs   ; the RST routines go down into page zero
04C8   11 08 00               LD   DE,0008h   
04CB   01 2C 00               LD   BC,vecend-vecs   
04CE   ED B0                  LDIR      
04D0                          ENDIF      
04D0                          IF   CPM*EDITOR   
                              CALL   load   ; the file named on the command line
                              JP   edit0   
04D0                          ENDIF      
04D0                          IF   CPM*(1-EDITOR)   
04D0   11 5C 00               LD   DE,005Ch   ; open the file named on the command line
04D3   0E 0F                  LD   C,15   ; (no such file: the first read fails too,
04D5   CD 05 00               CALL   BDOS   ;   and the program is empty)
04D8   11 00 08               LD   DE,PROG   
04DB   D5           LD1:      PUSH   DE   
04DC   0E 1A                  LD   C,26   ; set the DMA address
04DE   CD 05 00               CALL   BDOS   
04E1   11 5C 00               LD   DE,005Ch   
04E4   0E 14                  LD   C,20   ; read the next 128 bytes
04E6   CD 05 00               CALL   BDOS   
04E9   E1                     POP   HL   ; HL = the address this record went to
04EA   B7                     OR   A   
04EB   20 07                  JR   NZ,ld2   
04ED   11 80 00               LD   DE,128   
04F0   19                     ADD   HL,DE   
04F1   EB                     EX   DE,HL   
04F2   18 E7                  JR   ld1   
04F4   36 00        LD2:      LD   (HL),0   ; the end of the file counts as NUL
04F6   23                     INC   HL   ; the heap starts after it
04F7   01 00 08               LD   BC,PROG   ; the IP
04FA   C3 70 01               JP   st2   
04FD                          ENDIF      
04FD                          IF   CPM   
04FD                             ; RAM pages, after the image
04FD                RSPAGE:   EQU   (imgend + 255) / 256   
04FD                DSPAGE:   EQU   RSPAGE + 1   
04FD                LETPAGE:   EQU   RSPAGE + 2   
04FD                PROG:     EQU   LETPAGE*256 + 256   
04FD                          ENDIF      
04FD                IMGEND:      


